'''Oscar Jack Piastri''' ({{IPAc-en|p|i|ˈ|æ|s|t|r|iː}} {{Respell|pee|AST|ree}}, {{IPA|it|ˈpjastri|lang}}; born 6 April 2001) is an Australian [[racing driver]] who competes in [[Formula One]] for [[McLaren]]. Piastri has won {{Number to word|{{F1stat|PIA|wins}}}} [[Formula One Grands Prix]] across four seasons.

Born and raised in Melbourne, Piastri began his career in [[radio-controlled car|radio-controlled racing]] before moving into [[karting]] aged 10, where he won several regional titles. Graduating to [[junior formulae]] in 2016, Piastri won his first championship at the [[2019 Formula Renault Eurocup]] with [[R-ace GP]]. He then won both the [[2020 FIA Formula 3 Championship|2020 FIA Formula 3]] and [[2021 Formula 2 Championship|2021 FIA Formula 2]] Championships back-to-back with [[Prema Racing|Prema]], becoming the sixth driver in history to win the [[GP2 Series|GP2]]/[[FIA Formula 2 Championship|Formula 2]] title in their rookie season. Piastri is the only driver in history to win [[Formula Renault]], [[Formula Three]], and [[Formula Two]]—or equivalent—championships in successive seasons.

A member of the [[Alpine Academy]] from 2020 to 2022,{{efn-num|Known until 2021 as the ''Renault Sport Academy''.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/guanyu-zhou-spearheads-five-driver-alpine-academy-line-up-for-2021.6t6Ls79qFgitO7v6j0RSZ2 |title=Guanyu Zhou spearheads five-driver Alpine Academy line-up for 2021 |date=10 February 2021 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250214233352/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/guanyu-zhou-spearheads-five-driver-alpine-academy-line-up-for-2021.6t6Ls79qFgitO7v6j0RSZ2 |archive-date=14 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>|name=RSA}} Piastri signed with [[McLaren]] in {{F1|2023}} to partner [[Lando Norris]], following a contract dispute with [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]]. He made his Formula One debut at the {{F1GP|2023|Bahrain}}, achieving his first career podium in his rookie season at the {{F1GP|2023|Japanese}}. Retaining his [[Glossary of motorsport terms#S|seat]] for {{F1|2024}}, Piastri achieved his maiden [[List of Formula One Grand Prix winners|victory]] in [[2024 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]], which he repeated in [[2024 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan]], becoming the [[Formula One drivers from Australia#World champions and race winners|fifth Australian to win a Formula One Grand Prix]]. In {{F1|2025}}, he took seven further victories, as well as his maiden [[List of Formula One polesitters|pole position]] at the {{F1GP|2025|Chinese}}, as he finished third in a title battle with Norris and [[Max Verstappen]].

As of the [[{{F1stat|UPTO}}]], Piastri has achieved {{number to word|{{F1stat|PIA|wins}}}} race wins, {{number to word|{{F1stat|PIA|poles}}}} pole positions, {{number to word|{{F1stat|PIA|fastestlaps}}}} fastest laps, and {{F1stat|PIA|podiums}} podiums in Formula One. Piastri is contracted to remain at McLaren until at least the end of the 2028 season.

== Early life ==
[[File:Blancpain Gt Series Endurance Cup - Autodromo Nazionale di Monza - 22-04-2018 (41776555581).jpg|thumb|left|Piastri was sponsored by his father's company, ''HP Tuners'', throughout his [[junior formulae]] career.|alt=Piastri's Tatuus FR2.0/13 in the paddock of the 2018 Eurocup Formula Renault Monza round with its nose folded upwards]]
Oscar Jack Piastri was born on 6 April 2001 in Melbourne.<ref name="RS2025"/> His father, Chris Piastri, is the founder and owner of ''HP Tuners'', an [[vehicle diagnostics|automotive software]] company; the company sponsored his [[junior formulae]] career with up to {{currency|6.5|AUD}} million.<ref name="SMH2021">{{Cite news |url=https://www.smh.com.au/sport/motorsport/talent-nerve-and-cash-lots-of-cash-oscar-piastri-s-6-5m-formula-1-dream-20211207-p59ffq.html |url-access=subscription |title=Talent, nerve and lots of cash: F2 champion Oscar Piastri's $6.5m F1 dream |last=Lynch |first=Michael |date=11 December 2021 |work=[[The Sydney Morning Herald]] |publisher=[[Nine Entertainment]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |issn=0312-6315 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241213053432/https://www.smh.com.au/sport/motorsport/talent-nerve-and-cash-lots-of-cash-oscar-piastri-s-6-5m-formula-1-dream-20211207-p59ffq.html |archive-date=13 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He served as Piastri's [[kart]] mechanic as he contested [[List of kart racing championships#Australia|national championships in Australia]].<ref name="NYT2023"/> His mother, Nicole Piastri ({{nee}} MacFadyen), helped raise him in the suburb of [[Brighton, Victoria|Brighton]] with his three younger sisters—Hattie, Edie, and Mae.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/mar/13/formula-one-oscar-piastri-mclaren-f1-drivers-championship-contenders |title='I enjoy being the hunted': Oscar Piastri takes his place among F1 title contenders |last=Snape |first=Jack |date=13 March 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250407004649/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/mar/13/formula-one-oscar-piastri-mclaren-f1-drivers-championship-contenders |archive-date=7 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claims [[Italians|Italian]], [[Yugoslavs|Yugoslavian]], and [[Chinese people|Chinese]] heritage from his father, as well as [[Scottish people|Scottish]] and [[Irish people|Irish]] from his mother.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.repubblica.it/sport/formulauno/2025/04/14/news/piastri_mclaren_f1_gp_bahrein-424126973/ |url-access=subscription |title=Piastri, la missione Mondiale del pilota che vince con la testa |trans-title=Piastri, the World Championship mission of the driver who wins with his head |last=Retico |first=Alessandra |date=14 April 2025 |work=[[la Repubblica]] |publisher=[[GEDI Gruppo Editoriale]] |language=it |issn=0390-1076 |access-date=23 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250415034529/https://www.repubblica.it/sport/formulauno/2025/04/14/news/piastri_mclaren_f1_gp_bahrein-424126973/ |archive-date=15 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> His bedtime stories frequently consisted of automotive books, prompting his father to buy him a [[radio-controlled car]] on a business trip when he was six, which he began racing in his backyard.<ref name="RS2025">{{Cite magazine |url=https://au.rollingstone.com/culture/culture-features/oscar-piastri-basic-instinct-73836/ |title=Oscar Piastri's Basic Instinct |last=Yates |first=Rod |date=13 March 2025 |magazine=[[Rolling Stone Australia]] |publisher=[[Vinyl Group]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |issn=2652-5194 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250617204130/https://au.rollingstone.com/culture/culture-features/oscar-piastri-basic-instinct-73836/ |archive-date=17 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Piastri began racing competitively aged nine with ''Remote Control Racing Australia'', winning the secondary class of the national championship before moving into [[kart racing]].<ref name="AS2024"/><ref name="FA2024"/> Aged 14, he moved with his father—who returned to Melbourne six months later—to Hertford, England, to continue his international racing career in Europe.<ref name="RS2025"/> Having been privately educated at [[Haileybury (Melbourne)|Haileybury]], he moved to [[Haileybury and Imperial Service College|its sister school]] in [[Hertford Heath]]—whose [[List of people educated at Haileybury and Imperial Service College|alumni]] include [[Stirling Moss]]—as a [[boarding pupil]] on a [[sports scholarship]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-03-31/oscar-piastri-formula-1-career-grand-prix-starting-grid/102172834 |title=How Oscar Piastri's Formula 1 career might not have reached the starting grid |last=Conifer |first=Dan |date=31 March 2023 |work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250127093118/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-03-31/oscar-piastri-formula-1-career-grand-prix-starting-grid/102172834 |archive-date=27 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/07/05/meet-oscar-piastri-world-champion-to-be-schooled-in-england/ |url-access=registration |title=Oscar Piastri interview: The world champion hopeful schooled in England |last=Cary |first=Tom |date=5 July 2025 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |issn=0307-1235 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250707235630/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/07/05/meet-oscar-piastri-world-champion-to-be-schooled-in-england/ |archive-date=7 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> By the end of 2015, Piastri began travelling for karting tests and competitions between Italy, France, Belgium, Sweden, Spain, and Portugal from [[Stansted Airport]], costing his father around {{currency|250,000|GBP}}.<ref name="SMH2021"/> In [[2019 Formula Renault Eurocup|2019]], he was taken under the wing of nine-time Grand Prix winner [[Mark Webber (racing driver)|Mark Webber]] and his wife, Ann; the former has served as his [[sports agent|manager]] since and negotiated his move to Formula One.<ref name="AS2025-1">{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mark-webbers-influence-key-as-oscar-piastri-impresses-max-verstappen/10715870/ |title=How Webber's influence is key to Piastri impressing Verstappen |last=Hunt |first=Ben |date=22 April 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250426160650/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mark-webbers-influence-key-as-oscar-piastri-impresses-max-verstappen/10715870/ |archive-date=26 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

== Junior racing career ==
=== Karting (2011–2016) ===
==== 2011–2015: State titles in Australia ====
Following his successes in [[radio-controlled car|radio-controlled racing]], Piastri moved into [[kart racing]] in 2011 at the local ''Oakleigh Go Kart Racing Club'' (OGKRC) in [[Clayton South]], aged 10.<ref name="SC2023"/><ref name="FA2024">{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.forbes.com.au/news/30-under-30/inside-oscar-piastris-meteoric-f1-rise/ |title=How Oscar Piastri turned a remote-control-car hobby into a lucrative F1 career |last=Santoreneos |first=Anastasia |date=14 October 2024 |magazine=[[Forbes Australia]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0015-6914 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250524004841/https://www.forbes.com.au/news/30-under-30/inside-oscar-piastris-meteoric-f1-rise/ |archive-date=24 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> A protégé of two-time Australian Champion James Sera,<ref name="AS2024">{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-talent-spotters-that-moulded-piastri-into-an-f1-winner/10663046/ |title=The talent spotters that moulded Piastri into an F1 winner |last=Hunt |first=Ben |date=16 October 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241031085301/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-talent-spotters-that-moulded-piastri-into-an-f1-winner/10663046/ |archive-date=31 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> he began competing for the club that year in an [[FA Kart]] chassis.<ref name="NYT2023">{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4650146/2023/06/29/oscar-piastri-mclaren-rookie-f1/ |title=Home cooking and 'Call of Duty': Rookie Oscar Piastri rises as F1's everyman |last=Coleman |first=Madeline |date=29 June 2023 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241226162647/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4650146/2023/06/29/oscar-piastri-mclaren-rookie-f1/ |archive-date=26 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.vroomkart.com/news/42591/piastris-first-podium-in-f1-what-kind-of-kart-driver-was-he |title=Piastri's first podium in F1: what kind of kart driver was he? |last=Marangon |first=Fabio |date=25 September 2023 |magazine=Vroomkart |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=1724-9147 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240803000106/https://www.vroomkart.com/news/42591/piastris-first-podium-in-f1-what-kind-of-kart-driver-was-he |archive-date=3 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He won his first title two years later: the 2013 [[Commission Internationale de Karting|CIK]] Stars of Karting in the Rookies class.<ref name="NYT2023"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.mclaren.com/racing/team/oscar-piastri/ |title=Oscar Piastri |website=[[McLaren]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250623022611/https://www.mclaren.com/racing/team/oscar-piastri/ |archive-date=23 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> In 2014, he won the OGKRC Championship, City of Melbourne Titles, [[South Australia]]n Championship, and National Sprint Classic Champion of Champions in Junior Clubman—he claimed a {{currency|500|AUD}} prize for the latter.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://ogkrc.com.au/2022/09/oscar-piastri-joins-mclaren-f1/ |title=Oscar Piastri Joins McLaren F1 |last=Todd |first=Rafe |date=5 September 2022 |website=Oakleigh Go Kart Racing Club |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250614234927/https://ogkrc.com.au/2022/09/oscar-piastri-joins-mclaren-f1/ |archive-date=14 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/formula-1-2023-oscar-piastri-reflects-on-crazy-journey-from-karting-to-mclaren-20230714-p5j61a.html |title=Aussie young gun Oscar Piastri reflects on 'crazy' rise from $500 karting win to Formula 1 big bucks |last=Gates |first=Zachary |date=13 July 2023 |website=[[Nine's Wide World of Sports]] |publisher=[[Nine Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240807040047/https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/formula-1-2023-oscar-piastri-reflects-on-crazy-journey-from-karting-to-mclaren-20230714-p5j61a.html |archive-date=7 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.karting.net.au/piastri-to-make-european-debut/ |title=Piastri To Make European Debut |date=26 September 2014 |website=Karting Australia |publisher=[[Motorsport Australia]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250425024346/https://www.karting.net.au/piastri-to-make-european-debut/ |archive-date=25 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He further claimed runner-up in the Australian National Sprint Championship and the [[Victoria (state)|Victoria]]n Championship, before progressing to [[List of kart racing championships#Active international championships|international competition]] in the IAME International Final at [[Circuit de la Sarthe|Le Mans]]; he finished third on his debut in X30 Junior from twenty-first on the [[Glossary of motorsport terms#G|grid]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.karting.net.au/go-kart-oscar-piastris-podium-finish-international-debut-from-weekly-review/ |title=Oscar Piastri's podium finish for international debut – From the ''Weekly Review'' |date=10 November 2014 |website=Karting Australia |publisher=[[Motorsport Australia]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250425224126/https://www.karting.net.au/go-kart-oscar-piastris-podium-finish-international-debut-from-weekly-review/ |archive-date=25 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He closed his national career with third in the [[KF3]] Australian Championship—where he was ranked the ''Top Qualifier''—as well as victory in the Victorian Championship, OGKRC's Junior Top Guns, the [[Gold Coast, Queensland|Gold Coast]] Race of Stars, and the City of Melbourne Titles again in 2015.<ref name="BRDC">{{Cite web |url=http://www.brdc.co.uk/Oscar-Piastri |title=Oscar Piastri |website=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220713095904/http://www.brdc.co.uk/Oscar-Piastri |archive-date=13 July 2022 |url-status=dead}}</ref><ref name="KAU2015"/>

==== 2015–2016: Move to the European scene ====
{{quote box|quote=I knew it was a necessary step if I wanted to have a chance to make it to Formula One; you can't become a Formula One driver by staying in Australia.|source=—Piastri discussing his move to Europe with ''[[The New York Times]]'' in 2023<ref name="NYT2023"/>|width=30%|align=right|fontsize=85%}}
With the support of Sera and [[Scout (sport)|talent scout]] Rob McIntyre, Piastri moved to compete in [[List of kart racing championships#Europe|Europe]] from 2015 onwards with [[Kosmic Kart|Kosmic]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.karting.net.au/piastri-returns-to-europe-for-2015-campaign/ |title=Piastri returns to Europe for 2015 campaign |date=29 January 2015 |website=Karting Australia |publisher=[[Motorsport Australia]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250420072128/https://www.karting.net.au/piastri-returns-to-europe-for-2015-campaign/ |archive-date=20 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="AS2024"/> ''Vroomkart'' later contrasted his career path to that of [[Ayrton Senna]], having both progressed from RC racing to European karting after a transcontinental move.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.vroomkart.com/news/45092/senna-more-in-common-with-piastri-than-with-verstappen |title=Senna: more in common with Piastri than with Verstappen |last=Marangon |first=Fabio |date=1 May 2025 |magazine=Vroomkart |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=1724-9147 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250701063714/https://www.vroomkart.com/news/45092/senna-more-in-common-with-piastri-than-with-verstappen |archive-date=1 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> In [[KF-Junior]], he claimed twelfth in the [[Karting European Championship|European Championship]] round at [[Algarve International Circuit|Portimão]]—where he finished twenty-sixth overall—and entered one round of the [[WSK Super Master Series]].<ref name="FS2017"/><ref name="KAU2015">{{Cite web |url=https://www.karting.net.au/oscar-piastri-joins-ricky-flynn-motorsport-in-2016/ |title=Oscar Piastri joins Ricky Flynn Motorsport in 2016 |date=18 November 2015 |website=Karting Australia |publisher=[[Motorsport Australia]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250427011739/https://www.karting.net.au/oscar-piastri-joins-ricky-flynn-motorsport-in-2016/ |archive-date=27 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> In 2016, he returned to Australia to claim his third successive City of Melbourne Titles.<ref name="BRDC"/> In Europe, he joined ''Ricky Flynn Motorsport'' in [[OK-Junior]],<ref name="KAU2015"/> where he finished tenth in the South Garda Winter Cup, twelfth in the WSK Super Master Series, and eighth in the [[WSK Final Cup]].<ref name="FS2017">{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/scout-report-oscar-piastri/38005 |title=Scout Report: Oscar Piastri |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=30 August 2017 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250627001214/https://formulascout.com/scout-report-oscar-piastri/38005 |archive-date=27 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.mclaren.com/racing/formula-1/2024/oscar-piastri-road-to-victory/ |title=Oscar Piastri's road to victory in F1 |date=22 July 2024 |website=[[McLaren]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250519081635/https://www.mclaren.com/racing/formula-1/2024/oscar-piastri-road-to-victory/ |archive-date=19 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Back-to-back [[Podium#In motorsport|podium]]s at Portimão saw him claim sixteenth in the European Championship.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2016/06/27/portimao-the-turning-point-of-the-season/ |title=Portimão: the turning point of the season |date=27 June 2016 |website=Kartcom |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722085555/https://www.kartcom.com/en/news/2016/06/27/portimao-the-turning-point-of-the-season/ |archive-date=22 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.kartsportnews.com/c16/news_160803-4.html |title=CIK-FIA European Championship Final |date=3 August 2016 |website=KartSportNews |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230107205134/https://www.kartsportnews.com/c16/news_160803-4.html |archive-date=7 January 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified fourth for the [[Karting World Championship|World Championship]] at [[Bahrain International Circuit|Sakhir]] after winning his [[Glossary of motorsport terms#H|heat]]; his pre-final saw him drop to eighteenth before recovering to finish sixth overall in his final karting appearance.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://tkart.it/en/news/events/cik-fia-world-championship-junior-world-championship-sakhir-brn-qualifying-heas |title=CIK-FIA World Championship & Junior World Championship at Sakhir (Brn) – Qualifying heats |date=18 November 2016 |website=TKART |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722085936/https://tkart.it/en/news/events/cik-fia-world-championship-junior-world-championship-sakhir-brn-qualifying-heas |archive-date=22 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.karting.net.au/oscar-piastri-sixth-in-world-championship/ |title=Oscar Piastri sixth in World Championship |date=21 November 2016 |website=Karting Australia |publisher=[[Motorsport Australia]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250523205149/https://www.karting.net.au/oscar-piastri-sixth-in-world-championship/ |archive-date=23 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Formula 4 (2016–2017) ===
==== 2016–2017: Junior formulae debut in the UAE ====
Following his sixth-place at the [[Karting World Championship]] in [[OK-Junior]], Piastri made his [[junior formulae]] debut in the second round of the [[2016–17 Formula 4 UAE Championship|Formula 4 UAE Championship]] at [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]] with Dragon F4;<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/teenage-aussie-karter-make-uae-f4-debut/ |title=Teenage Aussie karter to make UAE F4 debut |date=15 December 2016 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250725103918/https://speedcafe.com/teenage-aussie-karter-make-uae-f4-debut/ |archive-date=25 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> in a nine-driver field, he claimed sixth, fifth, fourth, and fifth on debut.<ref name="FS2022">{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/the-timeline-of-oscar-piastris-journey-to-an-f1-seat/98074 |title=The timeline of Oscar Piastri's journey to an F1 seat |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=22 November 2022 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250219211104/https://formulascout.com/the-timeline-of-oscar-piastris-journey-to-an-f1-seat/98074 |archive-date=19 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="F4UAE17"/> He then scored a pair of fourth-places at [[Dubai Autodrome|Dubai]] before claiming two podiums on his return to Yas Marina—his final appearance in the series, ending the season sixth overall having contested 11 of 18 races.<ref name="F4UAE17"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/oscar-piastri-scores-double-podium-uae-f4/ |title=Oscar Piastri scores double podium in UAE F4 |date=13 February 2017 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250725104117/https://speedcafe.com/oscar-piastri-scores-double-podium-uae-f4/ |archive-date=25 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SC2023"/>

==== 2017: Runner-up in British F4 ====
[[File:Oscar Piastri - 2017 British F4 Knockhill (Sunday, R4) (cropped).jpg|thumb|left|Piastri finished runner-up to [[Jamie Caroline]] in his rookie [[2017 F4 British Championship|British F4]] season.|alt=Piastri driving the Mygale M14-F4 during the 2017 F4 British Championship]]
Piastri moved to the [[F4 British Championship]] for [[2017 F4 British Championship|2017]] with [[Arden International|Arden]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/arden-names-four-drivers-for-british-f4/36530 |title=Arden names four drivers for British F4 |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=8 February 2017 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250213223937/https://formulascout.com/arden-names-four-drivers-for-british-f4/36530 |archive-date=13 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> owned by [[Christian Horner]]—who later revealed he turned down the chance to sign Piastri to the [[Red Bull Junior Team]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12702941/oscar-piastri-red-bull-boss-christian-horner-regrets-not-taking-option-to-look-at-australian-driver |title=Oscar Piastri: Red Bull boss Christian Horner 'regrets' not taking option to look at Australian driver |date=22 September 2022 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221029143138/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12702941/oscar-piastri-red-bull-boss-christian-horner-regrets-not-taking-option-to-look-at-australian-driver |archive-date=29 October 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> He opened his campaign with two podiums at [[Brands Hatch]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/jamie-caroline-begins-british-f4-season-with-two-wins/36870 |title=Jamie Caroline begins British F4 season with two wins |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=2 April 2017 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250324032659/https://formulascout.com/jamie-caroline-begins-british-f4-season-with-two-wins/36870 |archive-date=24 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> which he repeated in the third race at [[Donington Park]], marred by the accident of [[Billy Monger]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/caroline-takes-two-more-british-f4-wins-monger-hurt-in-crash/36994 |title=Caroline takes two more British F4 wins, Monger hurt in crash |date=16 April 2017 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250619130213/https://formulascout.com/caroline-takes-two-more-british-f4-wins-monger-hurt-in-crash/36994 |archive-date=19 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-leicestershire-39651283 |title=Billy Monger crash: F4 driver's leg loss 'heart-wrenching' |date=20 April 2017 |work=[[BBC News]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250715075109/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-leicestershire-39651283 |archive-date=15 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After another podium at [[Thruxton Circuit|Thruxton]],<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2017/05/08/podium-for-aussie-piastri-in-british-f4 |title=Podium for Aussie Piastri in British F4 |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=8 May 2017 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180425154828/https://autoaction.com.au/2017/05/08/podium-for-aussie-piastri-in-british-f4 |archive-date=25 April 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> he claimed his maiden F4 victory in the second race at [[Oulton Park]] to move second in the championship.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/oscar-piastri-im-no-no2-im-here-to-become-world-champion-85jssj58c |url-access=subscription |title=Oscar Piastri: I'm no No2, I'm here to become world champion |last=Hudson |first=Molly |date=28 March 2025 |work=[[The Times]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |issn=0140-0460 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406100317/https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/oscar-piastri-im-no-no2-im-here-to-become-world-champion-85jssj58c |archive-date=6 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-wins-alex-peroni-oscar-piastri/ |title=World Wrap: Wins for Peroni and Piastri |date=22 May 2017 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240625155635/https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-wins-alex-peroni-oscar-piastri/ |archive-date=25 June 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Podiums in each race at [[Croft Circuit|Croft]] and two victories from [[pole position]] each at [[Snetterton Circuit|Snetterton]] and [[Knockhill]] consolidated his position.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2017/06/12/international-wrap-wrc-italy-aussies-overseas |title=International wrap: WRC Italy & Aussies overseas |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=12 June 2017 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180425152236/https://autoaction.com.au/2017/06/12/international-wrap-wrc-italy-aussies-overseas |archive-date=25 April 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-piastri-picks-two-wins/ |title=World Wrap: Piastri picks up two more wins |date=14 August 2017 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241010151237/https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-piastri-picks-two-wins/ |archive-date=10 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He came under pressure from [[Logan Sargeant]] after two retirements at [[Rockingham Motor Speedway|Rockingham]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/logan-sargeant-secures-first-british-formula-4-win-in-rockingham-finale/37989 |title=Logan Sargeant secures first British Formula 4 win in Rockingham finale |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=27 August 2017 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250207054117/https://formulascout.com/logan-sargeant-secures-first-british-formula-4-win-in-rockingham-finale/37989 |archive-date=7 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> A triple podium at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]], including victory in the final race, extended his advantage,<ref name="AA-SIL">{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2023/07/05/piastris-history-with-silverstone |title=Piastri's history with Silverstone |last=Neal |first=Timothy |date=5 July 2023 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250707040024/https://autoaction.com.au/2023/07/05/piastris-history-with-silverstone |archive-date=7 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://brscc.co.uk/piastri-sargeant-take-british-f4-down-to-the-wire/ |title=Piastri & Sargeant take British F4 down to the wire |last=McErlean |first=Paul |date=18 September 2017 |website=[[British Racing and Sports Car Club]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250513165034/https://brscc.co.uk/piastri-sargeant-take-british-f4-down-to-the-wire/ |archive-date=13 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> before he clinched the runner-up spot to the second-year [[Jamie Caroline]] with top-five finishes at Brands Hatch.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-piastri-runner-british-f4/ |title=World Wrap: Piastri runner-up in British F4 |date=2 October 2017 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250725111305/https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-piastri-runner-british-f4/ |archive-date=25 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He closed the season on 376.5 points—20.5 ahead of Sargeant and 65.5 behind Caroline—with six victories from 15 podiums and six pole positions.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/british-formula-4-2017-season-review/39322 |title=British Formula 4 2017 season review |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=22 December 2017 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241227184154/https://formulascout.com/british-formula-4-2017-season-review/39322 |archive-date=27 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He later credited "learning from [his] mistakes in F4" as his greatest lesson in [[junior formulae]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://fiaformula4.com/f2-star-piastri-reflects-on-oscar-winning-championship/ |title=F2 star Piastri reflects on 'Oscar'-winning championship |date=4 November 2021 |website=[[F4 British Championship]] |publisher=[[Motorsport UK]] |access-date=25 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250515230433/https://fiaformula4.com/f2-star-piastri-reflects-on-oscar-winning-championship/ |archive-date=15 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Formula Renault 2.0 (2017–2019) ===
==== 2017: Northern European Cup debut ====
Following his [[2017 F4 British Championship|British F4]] campaign, Piastri debuted in the [[2017 Formula Renault Northern European Cup|Formula Renault Northern European Cup]] at the season-ending [[Hockenheimring]] round with [[Arden International|Arden]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/piastri-lands-formula-renault-nec-drive/ |title=Piastri lands Formula Renault NEC drive |date=3 October 2017 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=13 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251013155004/https://speedcafe.com/piastri-lands-formula-renault-nec-drive/ |archive-date=13 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claimed eighth in both races, ending the season twenty-first overall.<ref name="FS2022"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.arden-motorsport.com/press/podium-for-vartanyan-and-piastri-stars-in-formula-renault-2-0-nec-debut |title=Podium for Vartanyan and Piastri stars in Formula Renault 2.0 NEC Debut |date=10 October 2017 |website=[[Arden International]] |access-date=13 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250623190339/https://www.arden-motorsport.com/press/podium-for-vartanyan-and-piastri-stars-in-formula-renault-2-0-nec-debut |archive-date=23 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="FRNEC17"/> He was subsequently invited to attend the [[Formula Renault 2.0]] rookie test at [[Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya|Barcelona-Catalunya]], setting the fifth-fastest time.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2017/11/01/oscar-piastri-impresses-formula-renault-rookie-test |title=Oscar Piastri impresses at Formula Renault rookie test |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=1 November 2017 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=13 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180422010612/https://autoaction.com.au/2017/11/01/oscar-piastri-impresses-formula-renault-rookie-test |archive-date=22 April 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2018: Podiums in the Eurocup ====
[[File:Blancpain Gt Series Endurance Cup - Autodromo Nazionale di Monza - 22-04-2018 (41650514132) (cropped2).jpg|thumb|right|In [[Formula Renault 2.0]], Piastri took three podiums across his [[Formula Renault Eurocup|Eurocup]] campaign in [[2018 Formula Renault Eurocup|2018]].|alt=Piastri driving the Tatuus FR2.0/13 at the 2018 Formula Renault Eurocup Monza round]]
Piastri remained with [[Arden International|Arden]] for his [[Formula Renault Eurocup|Eurocup]] debut in [[2018 Formula Renault Eurocup|2018]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.formulascout.com/british-f4-runner-up-oscar-piastri-to-step-up-to-fr2-0-eurocup-with-arden-motorsport/39618 |title=British F4 runner-up Oscar Piastri to step up to FR2.0 Eurocup with Arden Motorsport |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=20 December 2017 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250413103656/https://formulascout.com/british-f4-runner-up-oscar-piastri-to-step-up-to-fr2-0-eurocup-with-arden-motorsport/39618 |archive-date=13 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After claiming sixth and fifth on debut at [[Circuit Paul Ricard|Paul Ricard]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/sargeant-beats-fewtrell-to-win-eurocup-season-opener-at-paul-ricard/42169 |title=Sargeant beats Fewtrell to win Eurocup season opener at Paul Ricard |last=Waring |first=Bethonie |date=14 April 2018 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250212082230/https://formulascout.com/sargeant-beats-fewtrell-to-win-eurocup-season-opener-at-paul-ricard/42169 |archive-date=12 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/fr-20-c2-max-fewtrell-en-vainqueur-inconteste-193868.html |title=FR 2.0 – C2 : Max Fewtrell en vainqueur incontesté |trans-title=FR 2.0 – R2: Max Fewtrell as the undisputed winner |last=Satis |first=Jérémy |date=15 April 2018 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211205152018/https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/fr-20-c2-max-fewtrell-en-vainqueur-inconteste-193868.html |archive-date=5 December 2021 |url-status=live}}</ref> he scored no points at [[Monza Circuit|Monza]], including a retirement.<ref name="AA-MNZ"/> He finished fourth in the second race at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]] before dropping outside of the points again in [[Circuit de Monaco|Monaco]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://it.motorsport.com/frenault/news/max-fewtrell-e-charles-milesi-si-dividono-i-successi-a-silverstone-1039940/3097754/ |title=Max Fewtrell e Charles Milesi si dividono i successi a Silverstone |trans-title=Max Fewtrell and Charles Milesi share the wins at Silverstone |last=Di Marco |first=Marco |date=21 May 2018 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=it |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251016170018/https://it.motorsport.com/frenault/news/max-fewtrell-e-charles-milesi-si-dividono-i-successi-a-silverstone-1039940/3097754/ |archive-date=16 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-peroni-podium-monaco/ |title=World Wrap: Peroni on podium again in Monaco |last=Herrero |first=Daniel |date=28 May 2018 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251016170411/https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-peroni-podium-monaco/ |archive-date=16 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Following his sixth- and ninth-placed finishes at the [[Red Bull Ring]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-piastri-leads-aussies-in-renault-eurocup/ |title=World Wrap: Piastri leads Aussies in Renault Eurocup |last=Coch |first=Mat |date=23 July 2018 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240229073058/https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-piastri-leads-aussies-in-renault-eurocup/ |archive-date=29 February 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri achieved his maiden podium finish at [[Spa-Francorchamps]] with third in the opening race.<ref name="AA-SPA">{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2023/07/27/piastris-history-with-spa-francorchamps |title=Piastri's history with Spa Francorchamps |last=Neal |first=Timothy |date=27 July 2023 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=16 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251016201621/https://autoaction.com.au/2023/07/27/piastris-history-with-spa-francorchamps |archive-date=16 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Back-to-back points at the [[Hungaroring]] extended his run of points finishes to six races,<ref name="AA-HUN">{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2023/07/20/piastris-history-with-the-hungaroring |title=Piastri's history with the Hungaroring |last=Neal |first=Timothy |date=20 July 2023 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=16 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230721002449/https://autoaction.com.au/2023/07/20/piastris-history-with-the-hungaroring |archive-date=21 July 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> which ended in the first race at the [[Nürburgring]]; he claimed seventh in race two.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.arden-motorsport.com/press/arden-motorsport-score-at-the-nurburgring-in-formula-renault-eurocup |title=Arden Motorsport score at the Nürburgring in Formula Renault Eurocup |date=19 September 2018 |website=[[Arden International]] |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250624160950/https://www.arden-motorsport.com/press/arden-motorsport-score-at-the-nurburgring-in-formula-renault-eurocup |archive-date=24 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> With podiums in both races at the [[Hockenheimring]]—finishing third and second—he surpassed [[Alex Peroni]] for eighth in the championship,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-two-podiums-for-piastri-in-formula-renault/ |title=World Wrap: Two podiums for Piastri in Formula Renault |last=Herrero |first=Daniel |date=24 September 2018 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251016204358/https://speedcafe.com/world-wrap-two-podiums-for-piastri-in-formula-renault/ |archive-date=16 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> which he retained amidst non-scoring races at the season-ending [[Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya|Barcelona-Catalunya]] round.<ref name="FS2018">{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/max-fewtrell-crowned-formula-renault-eurocup-champion-as-logan-sargeant-wins-finale/45980 |title=Max Fewtrell crowned Formula Renault Eurocup champion as Logan Sargeant wins finale |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=21 October 2018 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=16 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250122042734/https://formulascout.com/max-fewtrell-crowned-formula-renault-eurocup-champion-as-logan-sargeant-wins-finale/45980 |archive-date=22 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He closed his campaign with 110 points—165.5 behind champion [[Max Fewtrell]]—and three podiums.<ref name="FS2018"/><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2022/09/23/horner-regrets-piastri-oversight-with-arden |title=Horner regrets team Arden's Piastri oversight |last=Neal |first=Timothy |date=23 September 2022 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=16 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220923051759/https://autoaction.com.au/2022/09/23/horner-regrets-piastri-oversight-with-arden |archive-date=23 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2019: Maiden title ====
[[File:Oscar Piastri Spa (cropped3).jpg|thumb|left|Piastri won the Eurocup in [[2019 Formula Renault Eurocup|2019]] amidst a title battle with [[Victor Martins]], his first junior championship.|alt=Piastri with his trophy and champagne after winning the 2019 Formula Renault Eurocup Spa-Francorchamps round]]
Piastri—now competing [[Motorsport UK|under a British licence]]—joined reigning champions {{nowrap|[[R-ace GP]]}} for the [[2019 Formula Renault Eurocup|2019 Eurocup]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2018/12/21/oscar-piastri-signs-with-formula-renault-champions |title=Oscar Piastri signs with Formula Renault champions |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=21 December 2018 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=18 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250911020235/https://autoaction.com.au/2018/12/21/oscar-piastri-signs-with-formula-renault-champions |archive-date=11 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.grandprix.com.au/fan-zone/news/five-moments-that-have-shaped-piastris-career |title=Five moments that have shaped Piastri's career |date=3 September 2022 |website=[[Australian Grand Prix]] |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251007172742/https://www.grandprix.com.au/fan-zone/news/five-moments-that-have-shaped-piastris-career |archive-date=7 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> His campaign opened with eighteenth and fourth at [[Monza Circuit|Monza]].<ref name="AA-MNZ"/> He took his maiden victory from [[pole position]] in the first race at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]], which he repeated in the second.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/oscar-piastri-signe-le-double-silverstone-en-fr-eurocup-202970.html |title=Oscar Piastri signe le doublé à Silverstone en FR Eurocup |trans-title=Oscar Piastri scores a double at Silverstone in the FR Eurocup |last=Tassel |first=Pierre |date=12 May 2019 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251019003254/https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/oscar-piastri-signe-le-double-silverstone-en-fr-eurocup-202970.html |archive-date=19 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claimed fourth and fifth in [[Circuit de Monaco|Monaco]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://motorsport.org.au/media/news/detail/2019/05/27/piastri-leads-aussie-monaco-assault-as-power-claims-solid-indy-500-result/ |title=Piastri and Power lead Aussie overseas charge |date=27 May 2019 |website=[[Motorsport Australia]] |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250418132929/https://motorsport.org.au/media/news/detail/2019/05/27/piastri-leads-aussie-monaco-assault-as-power-claims-solid-indy-500-result/ |archive-date=18 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> before returning to the podium with second at [[Circuit Paul Ricard|Paul Ricard]], where he finished sixth in race two.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://it.motorsport.com/frenault/news/colombo-si-esalta-in-francia-e-conquista-una-grande-doppietta-al-paul-ricard/4416159/ |title=Colombo si esalta in Francia e conquista una grande doppietta al Paul Ricard |trans-title=Colombo excels in France and wins a double at Paul Ricard |last=Di Marco |first=Marco |date=3 June 2019 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=it |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230725075225/https://it.motorsport.com/frenault/news/colombo-si-esalta-in-francia-e-conquista-una-grande-doppietta-al-paul-ricard/4416159/ |archive-date=25 July 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> He closed [[Victor Martins]]'s championship lead to two points with victory in the opening race at [[Spa-Francorchamps]] and levelled the standings with his fourth-place in race two.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2019/07/31/piastri-returns-to-top-of-standings-in-belgium |title=Piastri returns to top of standings in Belgium |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=31 July 2019 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=18 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251019004805/https://autoaction.com.au/2019/07/31/piastri-returns-to-top-of-standings-in-belgium |archive-date=19 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/colomb-wins-spa-eurocup/52767 |title=Lorenzo Colombo takes third 2019 Eurocup win in crash-shortened Spa race |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=27 July 2019 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250807031848/https://formulascout.com/colomb-wins-spa-eurocup/52767 |archive-date=7 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He opened a 40-point advantage by winning both races at the [[Nürburgring]] from pole.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/c1-piastri-solide-vainqueur-en-formule-renault-eurocup-au-nurburgring-205597.html |title=C1 – Piastri solide vainqueur en Formule Renault Eurocup au Nürburgring |trans-title=R1 – Piastri solid winner in Formula Renault Eurocup at the Nürburgring |last=Casaurang |first=Medhi |date=31 August 2019 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251019010426/https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/c1-piastri-solide-vainqueur-en-formule-renault-eurocup-au-nurburgring-205597.html |archive-date=19 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/piastr-dominates-eurocup-nurburgring/53923 |title=Piastri dominates at Nürburgring, single-seater returnee Quinn on Eurocup podium |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=1 September 2019 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240919170903/https://formulascout.com/piastr-dominates-eurocup-nurburgring/53923 |archive-date=19 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> A [[formation lap]] crash at the [[Hungaroring]] after [[aquaplaning]] reduced the gap by 12.5 points with Martins's victory,{{efn-num|[[Victor Martins]] was awarded half points for his victory in race one at the [[Hungaroring]] as the race was abandoned after three laps due to adverse weather conditions.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/victor-martins-wins-rained-off-formula-renault-eurocup-race-in-hungary/54137 |title=Victor Martins wins rained-off Formula Renault Eurocup race in Hungary |last=Waring |first=Bethonie |date=7 September 2019 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250419013856/https://formulascout.com/victor-martins-wins-rained-off-formula-renault-eurocup-race-in-hungary/54137 |archive-date=19 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>}} which he mitigated by winning the second race from pole.<ref name="AA-HUN"/> Martins closed his lead to 5.5 points with three consecutive wins from pole at the penultimate [[Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya|Barcelona-Catalunya]] and [[Hockenheimring]] rounds as Piastri finished fifth, third, and second, the latter after an early battle for the lead—his second-place in race two extended it by eight.<ref name="FS2019">{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/2019-formula-renault-season-review/57769 |title=2019 Formula Renault season review |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=23 December 2019 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241214090735/https://formulascout.com/2019-formula-renault-season-review/57769 |archive-date=14 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2019/10/08/piastri-maintains-lead-in-formula-renault-cup |title=Piastri maintains lead in Formula Renault Cup |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=8 October 2019 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=18 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251019141715/https://autoaction.com.au/2019/10/08/piastri-maintains-lead-in-formula-renault-cup |archive-date=19 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> At [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]], Piastri held off the late advances of Martins to win the opening race, meaning he would clinch the title by finishing seventh or higher in the final race, irrespective of other results.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.velocitymagazine.com.au/2019/10/29/oscar-piastri-crowned-2019-formula-renault-eurocup-champion/ |title=Oscar Piastri crowned 2019 Formula Renault Eurocup champion |date=29 October 2019 |magazine=Velocity Motorsport Magazine |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251019142029/https://www.velocitymagazine.com.au/2019/10/29/oscar-piastri-crowned-2019-formula-renault-eurocup-champion/ |archive-date=19 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> With fourth-place, Piastri clinched his first [[junior formulae]] championship by 7.5 points to Martins, having achieved seven wins from 11 podiums and five pole positions.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/c2-piastri-sacre-en-formule-renault-eurocup-malgre-le-succes-de-martins-206904.html |title=C2 – Piastri sacré en Formule Renault Eurocup malgré le succès de Martins |trans-title=R2 – Piastri crowned in Formula Renault Eurocup despite Martins's success |last=Casaurang |first=Medhi |date=26 October 2019 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |language=fr |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=18 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211028054253/https://www.autohebdo.fr/actualites/monoplace/c2-piastri-sacre-en-formule-renault-eurocup-malgre-le-succes-de-martins-206904.html |archive-date=28 October 2021 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="FS2019"/> Bruce Williams of ''[[Auto Action]]'' described it as a "a considerable step towards a Formula One career".<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2019/10/27/piastri-crowned-formula-renault-eurocup-champion |title=Piastri crowned Formula Renault Eurocup champion |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=27 October 2019 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=18 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231021123221/https://autoaction.com.au/2019/10/27/piastri-crowned-formula-renault-eurocup-champion |archive-date=21 October 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== FIA Formula 3 (2020) ===
In [[2018 GP3 Series|2018]], Piastri partook in the [[GP3 Series]] post-season test at [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]] with [[Trident Motorsport|Trident]].{{efn-num|The [[GP3 Series]] merged with the [[FIA Formula 3 European Championship]] to form the [[FIA Formula 3 Championship]] in {{FIAF3|2019}}.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/new-fia-f3-car-will-be-more-difficult-to-drive-than-gp3-machine-5283418/5283418/ |title=New FIA F3 car will be 'more difficult to drive' than GP3 machine |last1=Benyon |first1=Jack |last2=Evans |first2=David |date=4 February 2019 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250403190839/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/new-fia-f3-car-will-be-more-difficult-to-drive-than-gp3-machine-5283418/5283418/ |archive-date=3 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>}}<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2018/11/28/oscar-piastri-to-test-gp3-in-abu-dhabi |title=Oscar Piastri to test GP3 in Abu Dhabi |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=28 November 2018 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250413103657/https://autoaction.com.au/2018/11/28/oscar-piastri-to-test-gp3-in-abu-dhabi |archive-date=13 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He returned for the {{FIAF3|2019}} post-season test with reigning [[FIA Formula 3]] champions [[Prema Racing|Prema]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/fia-formula-3-championship/news/prema-valencia-test-lineup/4559601/ |title=Prema names F3 post-season test line-up |last=Benyon |first=Jack |date=18 October 2019 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250413103656/https://www.motorsport.com/fia-formula-3-championship/news/prema-valencia-test-lineup/4559601/ |archive-date=13 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Now [[Sports agent|managed]] by [[Mark Webber (racing driver)|Mark Webber]] and a member of the [[Renault Sport Academy]],<ref name="AS2025-1"/><ref name="MS2020"/> he signed with Prema for {{FIAF3|2020}} alongside former [[Formula 4|F4]] rival [[Logan Sargeant]] and reigning [[2019 Formula Regional European Championship|Formula Regional European]] champion [[Frederik Vesti]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/oscar-piastri-becomes-renault-junior-joins-prema-in-fia-f3/59054 |title=Oscar Piastri becomes Renault junior, joins Prema in FIA F3 |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=26 January 2020 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250426045144/https://formulascout.com/oscar-piastri-becomes-renault-junior-joins-prema-in-fia-f3/59054 |archive-date=26 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> The season was [[Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on motorsport#Formula 2 and Formula 3|delayed and shortened]] due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/how-f1s-feeder-series-dealt-with-covid-19-and-prepared-to-go-back-to-racing.5MrvBUcaoE3h9eYZzw716e |title=How F1's feeder series dealt with COVID-19 – and prepared to go back to racing |last=Stuart |first=Greg |date=5 June 2020 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250716021652/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/how-f1s-feeder-series-dealt-with-covid-19-and-prepared-to-go-back-to-racing.5MrvBUcaoE3h9eYZzw716e |archive-date=16 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Stating that "fighting for the championship definitely is not out of the question",<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/f1-2020-oscar-piastri-daniel-ricciardo-renault-sport-academy-prema-racing-20200316-p5ii5d.html |title=Exclusive: Aussie prodigy's world turned upside down |last=Graham |first=Brett |date=16 March 2020 |website=[[Nine's Wide World of Sports]] |publisher=[[Nine Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251023004847/https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/f1-2020-oscar-piastri-daniel-ricciardo-renault-sport-academy-prema-racing-20200316-p5ii5d.html |archive-date=23 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri qualified third on debut in [[2020 Spielberg Formula 3 round|Spielberg]]; avoiding damage in a first-corner collision with polesitter [[Sebastián Fernández (racing driver)|Sebastián Fernández]], he passed [[Lirim Zendeli]] at ''[[Red Bull Ring|Ams Ag]]'' to claim a debut [[FIA Formula 3 Championship#Race weekend|feature race]] victory,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/piastri-thought-debut-f3-race-had-ended-in-first-10-seconds/64100 |title=Piastri thought debut F3 race had ended "in first 10 seconds" |last=Wood |first=Ida |date=4 July 2020 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250413103657/https://formulascout.com/piastri-thought-debut-f3-race-had-ended-in-first-10-seconds/64100 |archive-date=13 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> before finishing eighth in the [[Glossary of motorsport terms#R|reverse-grid]] sprint.{{efn-num|In the [[2020 FIA Formula 3 Championship]], the top 10 finishers in the [[FIA Formula 3 Championship#Race weekend|feature race]] were subjected to a [[Glossary of motorsport terms#R|reverse-grid]] in the [[FIA Formula 3 Championship#Race weekend|sprint race]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/fia-f3-tweaks-points-system-and-reversed-grid-race-format-for-2020-4983875/4983875/ |title=FIA F3 tweaks points system and reversed-grid race format for 2020 |last=Khorounzhiy |first=Valentin |date=25 February 2020 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231129152214/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/fia-f3-tweaks-points-system-and-reversed-grid-race-format-for-2020-4983875/4983875/ |archive-date=29 November 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref>}}<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/liam-lawson-takes-maiden-fia-f3-win-in-red-bull-ring-race-two/64128 |title=Liam Lawson takes maiden FIA F3 race win in second Red Bull Ring race |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=5 July 2020 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240521035551/https://formulascout.com/liam-lawson-takes-maiden-fia-f3-win-in-red-bull-ring-race-two/64128 |archive-date=21 May 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> At the [[2020 2nd Spielberg Formula 3 round|second Spielberg round]], he claimed fourth in the curtailed feature and fifth in the sprint to retain his championship lead over Vesti and Sargeant.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/austria-rain-feature-race-vesti/4830852/ |title=Red Bull Ring F3: Vesti wins truncated feature race |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=11 July 2020 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230725151732/https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/austria-rain-feature-race-vesti/4830852/ |archive-date=25 July 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-pourchaire-becomes-youngest-ever-fia-f3-winner-in-sprint-race.4WEwUXtBhQ4gOQBAICde3z |title=Road to F1: Pourchaire becomes youngest-ever FIA F3 winner in sprint race |date=12 July 2020 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250812190500/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-pourchaire-becomes-youngest-ever-fia-f3-winner-in-sprint-race.4WEwUXtBhQ4gOQBAICde3z |archive-date=12 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Back-to-back second-placed finishes in [[2020 Budapest Formula 3 round|Budapest]]—as well as in the [[2020 Silverstone Formula 3 round|Silverstone]] feature—increased his advantage to 25 points, prior to losing eight with a [[drag reduction system]] failure in the latter sprint.<ref name="AA-HUN"/><ref name="AA-SIL"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-alex-smolyar-takes-his-first-f3-victory-to-become-sixth-different.15FQz8cI4Ikg7pNmhbZ7rp |title=Road to F1: Smolyar stripped of first F3 win after stewards penalise him for weaving |date=2 August 2020 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250710114424/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-alex-smolyar-takes-his-first-f3-victory-to-become-sixth-different.15FQz8cI4Ikg7pNmhbZ7rp |archive-date=10 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He fell a point behind Sargeant after claiming seventh and sixth at the [[2020 2nd Silverstone Formula 3 round|second Silverstone round]] following reliability issues in qualifying,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fia.com/news/f3-sargeant-steals-championship-lead-first-f3-win-ahead-hugues |title=F3 – Sargeant steals the championship lead with first F3 win ahead of Hughes |date=8 August 2020 |website=[[Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250807063928/https://www.fia.com/news/f3-sargeant-steals-championship-lead-first-f3-win-ahead-hugues |archive-date=7 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/silverstone-f3-viscaal-takes-maiden-series-win-after-thrilling-last-lap-duel-4980332/4980332/ |title=Silverstone F3: Viscaal takes maiden series win after thrilling last-lap duel |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=9 August 2020 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240613052820/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/silverstone-f3-viscaal-takes-maiden-series-win-after-thrilling-last-lap-duel-4980332/4980332/ |archive-date=13 June 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> which he retained in [[2020 Barcelona Formula 3 round|Barcelona]] by recovering from a sixth-placed feature to win the sprint, courtesy of four opening-lap overtakes.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-jake-hughes-takes-first-f3-feature-race-victory-in-spain.6KF39YsGP2LhdsrOK43HUP |title=Road to F1: Jake Hughes takes first F3 feature race victory in Spain |date=15 August 2020 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250712072808/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-jake-hughes-takes-first-f3-feature-race-victory-in-spain.6KF39YsGP2LhdsrOK43HUP |archive-date=12 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/oscar-piastri-formula-three-championship-belgium-prema-racing-title-race-logan-sargeant-exclusive-20200826-p5io93.html |title=Exclusive: Australia's Oscar Piastri eyes F3 title as season enters final three rounds |last=Graham |first=Brett |date=26 August 2020 |website=[[Nine's Wide World of Sports]] |publisher=[[Nine Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241102125301/https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/oscar-piastri-formula-three-championship-belgium-prema-racing-title-race-logan-sargeant-exclusive-20200826-p5io93.html |archive-date=2 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

At [[2020 Spa-Francorchamps Formula 3 round|Spa-Francorchamps]], Sargeant extended his lead to seven points over Piastri—who claimed fifth and sixth, the latter after a penalty for an illegal overtake on [[Richard Verschoor]]—with his sprint victory.<ref name="AA-SPA"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/spa-sprint-race-sargeant-piastri/4865540/ |title=Spa F3: Sargeant wins sprint race to reclaim points lead |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=30 August 2020 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241203141820/https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/spa-sprint-race-sargeant-piastri/4865540/ |archive-date=3 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri reclaimed the lead at the penultimate [[2020 Monza Formula 3 round|Monza]] round, where he climbed from fifteenth to third in the feature; he retired from the sprint after a collision with [[Clément Novalak]] and [[David Schumacher (racing driver)|David Schumacher]] at ''[[Monza Circuit|Variante del Rettifilo]]'', which was neutralised by Sargeant's late crash with Vesti.<ref name="AA-MNZ"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://jp.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/2020-fia-f3-monza2-report/4869469/ |title=F3モンツァ：レース2はヒューズが追い上げ2勝目飾る。プレマは全員がリタイア |trans-title=F3 Monza: Hughes makes a comeback in Race 2 to take his second win. All Prema drivers retire. |last=Nagayasu |first=Yosuke |date=6 September 2020 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=ja |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220925102748/https://jp.motorsport.com/fia-f3/news/2020-fia-f3-monza2-report/4869469/ |archive-date=25 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> Eight points above Sargeant and 24 above the [[ART Grand Prix|ART]] of [[Théo Pourchaire]] into the season-ending [[2020 Mugello Formula 3 round|Mugello]] round,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/28Q05bVPgyGNaF7sWknzmS/r0ad-to-100-piastri-wins-nail-bitter-as-prema-make-it-two-in-a-row |title=Road to 100: Piastri wins a nail-biter as PREMA make it two in a row |date=5 June 2024 |website=[[FIA Formula 3 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250522030040/https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/28Q05bVPgyGNaF7sWknzmS/r0ad-to-100-piastri-wins-nail-bitter-as-prema-make-it-two-in-a-row |archive-date=22 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri—carrying over a five-place [[Glossary of motorsport terms#G|grid penalty]] for forcing [[David Beckmann]] off-track—lined up sixteenth on the feature [[Glossary of motorsport terms#G|grid]];<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/zendeli-on-pole-for-f3-finale-at-mugello-points-leader-piastri-16th-4979207/4979207/ |title=Zendeli on pole for F3 finale at Mugello, points leader Piastri 16th |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=11 September 2020 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240617235223/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/zendeli-on-pole-for-f3-finale-at-mugello-points-leader-piastri-16th-4979207/4979207/ |archive-date=17 June 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> unable to score points in eleventh, he entered the sprint tied with Sargeant—who started fifth—and nine points clear of Pourchaire in eighth.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-vesti-wins-at-mugello-as-piastri-and-sargeant-are-tied-on-points.6sbkZUlEYLfinIzWSPm6Ly |title=Road to F1: Vesti wins at Mugello as Piastri and Sargeant are tied on points going into F3 finale |date=12 September 2020 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250810102539/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/road-to-f1-vesti-wins-at-mugello-as-piastri-and-sargeant-are-tied-on-points.6sbkZUlEYLfinIzWSPm6Ly |archive-date=10 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Sargeant was eliminated in a first-lap collision with Zendeli at ''[[Mugello Circuit|Luco]]'' as Piastri passed four drivers, including Pourchaire, for seventh.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/1pdOXASncCmdwPHqXvM24i/piastri-crowned-f3-champion-as-lawson-eases-to-third-win-of-the-year-in |title=Piastri crowned F3 champion, as Lawson eases to third win of the year in season finale |date=13 September 2020 |website=[[FIA Formula 3 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250805034907/https://www.fiaformula3.com/Latest/1pdOXASncCmdwPHqXvM24i/piastri-crowned-f3-champion-as-lawson-eases-to-third-win-of-the-year-in |archive-date=5 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Pourchaire reclaimed the position on the [[safety car]] restart, but was unable to close the gap with his podium as Piastri clinched seventh and the title.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/mugello-f3-piastri-wins-2020-title-as-lawson-dominates-season-finale-4979124/4979124/ |title=Mugello F3: Piastri wins 2020 title as Lawson dominates season finale |last=Suttill |first=Josh |date=13 September 2020 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250410065051/https://www.autosport.com/fia-f3/news/mugello-f3-piastri-wins-2020-title-as-lawson-dominates-season-finale-4979124/4979124/ |archive-date=10 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He closed his campaign on 164 points—three ahead of Pourchaire and four ahead of Sargeant—with two victories from six podiums.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.renaultsport.com/oscar-piastri-wins-2020-fia-formula-3-championship-title.html |title=Oscar Piastri wins 2020 FIA Formula 3 Championship title |date=13 September 2020 |website=[[Renault Sport]] |publisher=[[Renault]] |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211011173302/https://www.renaultsport.com/oscar-piastri-wins-2020-fia-formula-3-championship-title.html |archive-date=11 October 2021 |url-status=dead}}</ref> He credited improvements in his racecraft with helping him deal with the increased competition and subsequently became a Formula One [[test driver]] for [[Renault in Formula One|Renault]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/oscar-piastri-was-more-confident-of-fia-f3-title-than-eurocup-success/68164 |title=Oscar Piastri was more confident of FIA F3 title than Eurocup success |last=Allen |first=Peter |date=14 September 2020 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=22 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241208204631/https://formulascout.com/oscar-piastri-was-more-confident-of-fia-f3-title-than-eurocup-success/68164 |archive-date=8 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="AA2020"/>

=== FIA Formula 2 (2021) ===
[[File:2021 British Grand Prix (51349300361).jpg|thumb|right|In {{F2|2021}}, Piastri won the [[FIA Formula 2 Championship]] in his rookie season with [[Prema Racing|Prema]].|alt=Piastri driving the Dallara F2 2018 at the 2021 Silverstone Formula 2 round]]
Piastri remained with [[Prema Racing|Prema]] for his {{F2|2021}} campaign in [[FIA Formula 2]], replacing [[Mick Schumacher]] to partner [[Ferrari Driver Academy]] member [[Robert Shwartzman]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f2/news/prema-oscar-piastri-2021-renault/4919119/ |title=Prema signs F3 champion Piastri for 2021 F2 season |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=1 December 2020 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241014135229/https://www.motorsport.com/fia-f2/news/prema-oscar-piastri-2021-renault/4919119/ |archive-date=14 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He debuted in [[Formula Two]] machinery during the three-day {{F2|2020}} post-season test at [[Bahrain International Circuit|Sakhir]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5Fpaxoy71HJV0ogPE8KTKO/piastri-promoted-to-formula-2-in-2021-with-prema |title=Piastri promoted to Formula 2 in 2021 with PREMA |date=1 December 2020 |website=[[FIA Formula 2 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250121194933/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/5Fpaxoy71HJV0ogPE8KTKO/piastri-promoted-to-formula-2-in-2021-with-prema |archive-date=21 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Prior to the season, he stated that he was expecting a "very challenging year", with plans to remain in the category for two years.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://au.motorsport.com/fia-f2/news/piastri-rookie-f2-year-very-important-as-f1-looms-on-the-horizon/5381202/ |title=Piastri: Rookie F2 year "very important" as F1 looms on the horizon |last=Howard |first=Tom |date=11 February 2021 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250501012920/https://au.motorsport.com/fia-f2/news/piastri-rookie-f2-year-very-important-as-f1-looms-on-the-horizon/5381202/ |archive-date=1 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri qualified seventh on debut at [[2021 Sakhir Formula 2 round|Sakhir]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/zhou-snatches-bahrain-f2-pole-but-under-investigation-/5920043/ |title=Zhou snatches Bahrain F2 feature race pole, but under investigation |last=Howard |first=Tom |date=26 March 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230924224248/https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/zhou-snatches-bahrain-f2-pole-but-under-investigation-/5920043/ |archive-date=24 September 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/pourchaire-inherits-f2-pole-after-vips-disqualification/5924397/ |title=Pourchaire inherits F2 pole after Vips disqualification |last=Howard |first=Tom |date=26 March 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240713091534/https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/pourchaire-inherits-f2-pole-after-vips-disqualification/5924397/ |archive-date=13 July 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> finishing fifth in the [[Glossary of motorsport terms#R|reverse-grid]] first [[FIA Formula 2 Championship#Race weekend|sprint race]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/lawson-fends-off-daruvala-for-maiden-f2-win-in-bahrain/5936011/ |title=Lawson fends off Daruvala for maiden F2 win in Bahrain |last=Howard |first=Tom |date=27 March 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240713091531/https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/lawson-fends-off-daruvala-for-maiden-f2-win-in-bahrain/5936011/ |archive-date=13 July 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Starting sixth for the second sprint,{{efn-num|In the [[2021 FIA Formula 2 Championship]], the top 10 qualifiers were subjected to a [[Glossary of motorsport terms#R|reverse-grid]] in the first [[FIA Formula 2 Championship#Race weekend|sprint race]], the results of which were subjected to another reversal for the second sprint.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://formulascout.com/aiming-for-reversed-grid-pole-in-new-f2-format-unsportsmanlike-piastri/76707 |title=Aiming for reversed-grid pole in new F2 format 'unsportsmanlike' – Piastri |last=Woollard |first=Craig |date=26 March 2021 |website=Formula Scout |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241011030317/https://formulascout.com/aiming-for-reversed-grid-pole-in-new-f2-format-unsportsmanlike-piastri/76707 |archive-date=11 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>}} he took his maiden victory after seven overtakes in the closing seven laps, following a [[pit stop]] for [[Glossary of motorsport terms#O|option tyres]] behind the [[safety car]], claiming the lead from [[Zhou Guanyu]] on the final tour.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/piastri-calls-maiden-f2-win-craziest-ever/5952026/ |title=Piastri calls maiden F2 win 'craziest ever' |last=Howard |first=Tom |date=28 March 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231204165837/https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/piastri-calls-maiden-f2-win-craziest-ever/5952026/ |archive-date=4 December 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> He then made several overtakes to lead the [[FIA Formula 2 Championship#Race weekend|feature]], before retiring amidst a collision with [[Dan Ticktum]] while battling for third on the third from last lap.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2KxPFaIoNmlPKIuqbLYL0l/feature-race-zhou-fights-to-first-feature-race-win-with-inspired-performance |title=Feature Race: Zhou fights to first Feature Race win with inspired performance in Sakhir |date=28 March 2021 |website=[[FIA Formula 2 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250119190130/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/2KxPFaIoNmlPKIuqbLYL0l/feature-race-zhou-fights-to-first-feature-race-win-with-inspired-performance |archive-date=19 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Qualifying third in both [[2021 Monte Carlo Formula 2 round|Monte Carlo]] and [[2021 Baku Formula 2 round|Baku]],{{efn-num|Since [[2017 Monte Carlo Formula 2 round|2017]], qualifying for the [[Circuit de Monaco|Monte Carlo]] FIA Formula 2 round had been split into two groups; qualifying position in each group decided the starting [[Glossary of motorsport terms#G|grid-row]], with the order of each row decided by the fastest time between them.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2025/05/22/f2-monaco-preview-tight-margins-title-tensions-and-a-circuit-that-forgives-nothing |title=F2 Monaco Preview: Tight Margins, Title Tensions and a Circuit That Forgives Nothing |date=22 May 2025 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722033439/https://autoaction.com.au/2025/05/22/f2-monaco-preview-tight-margins-title-tensions-and-a-circuit-that-forgives-nothing |archive-date=22 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri qualified second in his group and, with a faster time than [[Dan Ticktum]], was classified third overall.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://acm.mc/formule-2-theo-pourchaire-un-debutant-en-pole-position/ |title=Formule 2 : Théo Pourchaire, un débutant en pole position ! |trans-title=Formula 2: Théo Pourchaire, a rookie on pole position! |date=20 May 2021 |website=[[Automobile Club de Monaco]] |language=fr |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250616035901/https://acm.mc/formule-2-theo-pourchaire-un-debutant-en-pole-position/ |archive-date=16 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>}} he claimed second in the second sprint and feature at the former, as well as the latter feature.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-lawson-fights-back-from-slow-start-to-take-wet-weather-win-in-monaco.7gvse9OoNZoaxFYExs0JVf |title=F2: Ticktum handed Monaco Sprint Race victory as Lawson is disqualified |date=22 May 2021 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250514135739/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-lawson-fights-back-from-slow-start-to-take-wet-weather-win-in-monaco.7gvse9OoNZoaxFYExs0JVf |archive-date=14 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/1g9t9Wx3k0dCq1ZUKhzRD0/feature-race |title=Feature Race: Pourchaire becomes F2's youngest-ever race-winner with inspired performance in Monte Carlo |date=22 May 2021 |website=[[FIA Formula 2 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250120142218/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/1g9t9Wx3k0dCq1ZUKhzRD0/feature-race |archive-date=20 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/490yohGXOKTjBJmecvJPxN/i-didnt-have-the-experience-of-where-to-brake-piastri-on-how-the-sprint-race |title='I didn't have the experience of where to brake' – Piastri on how the Sprint Race 1 retirement affected his weekend |date=8 June 2021 |website=[[FIA Formula 2 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250413103702/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/490yohGXOKTjBJmecvJPxN/i-didnt-have-the-experience-of-where-to-brake-piastri-on-how-the-sprint-race |archive-date=13 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Following his maiden [[pole position]] at [[2021 Silverstone Formula 2 round|Silverstone]], he finished sixth, fourth, and third to claim the championship lead from Zhou.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2021/07/18/piastri-takes-f2-championship-lead |title=Piastri takes F2 championship lead |last=McCarthy |first=Dan |date=18 July 2021 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722035715/https://autoaction.com.au/2021/07/18/piastri-takes-f2-championship-lead |archive-date=22 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://cn.motorsport.com/fia-f2/news/%E9%93%B6%E7%9F%B3f2%E4%B8%BB%E8%B5%9B%E5%91%A8%E5%86%A0%E5%AE%87%E5%BC%BA%E5%8A%BF%E5%8F%91%E8%BD%A6%E7%BB%9F%E6%B2%BB%E5%85%A8%E5%9C%BA%E8%8E%B7%E8%83%9C/6632821/ |title=银石F2主赛：周冠宇强势发车，统治全场获胜 |trans-title=Silverstone F2 Feature Race: Zhou Guanyu started strongly and won the race |date=18 July 2021 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |language=zh |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240721042919/https://cn.motorsport.com/fia-f2/news/%E9%93%B6%E7%9F%B3f2%E4%B8%BB%E8%B5%9B%E5%91%A8%E5%86%A0%E5%AE%87%E5%BC%BA%E5%8A%BF%E5%8F%91%E8%BD%A6%E7%BB%9F%E6%B2%BB%E5%85%A8%E5%9C%BA%E8%8E%B7%E8%83%9C/6632821/ |archive-date=21 July 2024 |url-status=live }}</ref>

After ending fourth and seventh in the [[2021 Monza Formula 2 round|Monza]] sprints, Piastri won the feature from pole in a battle with Zhou, which he repeated at [[2021 Sochi Formula 2 round|Sochi]] with [[Théo Pourchaire]].<ref name="AA-MNZ"/><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/f2-sochi-feature-race-piastri-beats-pourchaire-to-extend-lead/6675002/ |title=F2 Sochi: Piastri strengthens title push after dominant feature race victory |last=Howard |first=Tom |date=26 September 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231209182048/https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/f2-sochi-feature-race-piastri-beats-pourchaire-to-extend-lead/6675002/ |archive-date=9 December 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> He took two further victories at [[2021 Jeddah Formula 2 round|Jeddah]]: he won the second sprint and the feature from pole, the latter being aborted in the wake of several [[red flag (motorsport)|red flag]] incidents.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-12-06/oscar-piastri-wins-f2-race-two-drivers-airlifted-to-hospital/100676160 |title=Australian Oscar Piastri wins F2 race with two drivers airlifted to hospital |last=Doyle |first=Michael |date=5 December 2021 |work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240421091943/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-12-06/oscar-piastri-wins-f2-race-two-drivers-airlifted-to-hospital/100676160 |archive-date=21 April 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> His fifth consecutive pole at [[2021 Yas Island Formula 2 round|Yas Island]] saw him start tenth in the first sprint, where he claimed third in a late battle with teammate and runner-up Shwartzman to clinch the title;<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/f2-abu-dhabi-piastri-beats-doohan-to-claim-fifth-consecutive-pole/6870988/ |title=F2 Abu Dhabi: Piastri beats Doohan to claim fifth consecutive pole |last=Howard |first=Tom |date=10 December 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250124192804/https://www.autosport.com/formula2/news/f2-abu-dhabi-piastri-beats-doohan-to-claim-fifth-consecutive-pole/6870988/ |archive-date=24 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-12-11/australia-oscar-piastri-wins-formula-2-world-title/100693480 |title=Australia's Oscar Piastri wins Formula 2 world title in Abu Dhabi |date=11 December 2021 |work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230207123911/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2021-12-11/australia-oscar-piastri-wins-formula-2-world-title/100693480 |archive-date=7 February 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> he closed the season with his record fourth successive feature victory.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-piastri-caps-off-title-winning-season-with-feature-race-win-in-abu-dhabi.2jIf9HJxrLEwQpdwapDfJQ |title=F2: Piastri caps off title-winning season with Feature Race win in Abu Dhabi |date=12 December 2021 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250524221259/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/f2-piastri-caps-off-title-winning-season-with-feature-race-win-in-abu-dhabi.2jIf9HJxrLEwQpdwapDfJQ |archive-date=24 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Across his campaign, Piastri took 252.5 points—60.5 ahead of Shwartzman—with six wins from 11 podiums and five pole positions.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.canberratimes.com.au/story/7547555/f2-champ-piastri-ends-with-sixth-win/ |title=F2 champ Piastri ends with sixth win |last=Chadband |first=Ian |date=12 December 2021 |work=[[The Canberra Times]] |publisher=[[Australian Community Media]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=2653-0996 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722040539/https://www.canberratimes.com.au/story/7547555/f2-champ-piastri-ends-with-sixth-win/ |archive-date=22 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/piastri-rounds-out-f2-campaign-with-race-win/ |title=Piastri rounds out F2 campaign with race win |last=Coch |first=Mat |date=13 December 2021 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |publisher=[[Speedcafe|BAM Media Group]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240723184116/https://speedcafe.com/piastri-rounds-out-f2-campaign-with-race-win/ |archive-date=23 July 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He became the sixth driver in history to win the [[GP2 Series|GP2]]/F2 title in their rookie season,{{efn-num|In {{F2|2021}}, Piastri became the sixth driver in history to win the [[GP2 Series|GP2]]/[[FIA Formula 2 Championship|F2]] title in their rookie season, after: [[Nico Rosberg]] ([[2005 GP2 Series|2005]]), [[Lewis Hamilton]] ([[2006 GP2 Series|2006]]), [[Nico Hülkenberg]] ([[2009 GP2 Series|2009]]), [[Charles Leclerc]] ({{F2|2017}}), and [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]] ({{F2|2018}}).<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autohebdof1.com/news/car/2-formula/oscar-piastri-at-the-table-of-hamilton-rosberg-hulkenberg-leclerc-and-russell.html |title=Oscar Piastri at the table of Hamilton, Rosberg, Hülkenberg, Leclerc and Russell |last=Satis |first=Jeremy |date=11 December 2021 |magazine=Auto Hebdo |issn=0395-4366 |access-date=22 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250124035912/https://www.autohebdof1.com/news/car/2-formula/oscar-piastri-at-the-table-of-hamilton-rosberg-hulkenberg-leclerc-and-russell.html |archive-date=24 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>}} the third to win the [[GP3 Series|GP3]]/[[FIA Formula 3 Championship|F3]] and GP2/F2 titles in successive seasons,{{efn-num|In {{F2|2021}}, Piastri became the fifth driver in history to win the [[GP3 Series|GP3]]/[[FIA Formula 3 Championship|F3]] and [[GP2 Series|GP2]]/[[FIA Formula 2 Championship|F2]] titles in successive seasons, after: [[Charles Leclerc]] and [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2021/12/12/three-consecutive-titles-special-for-piastri |title=Three consecutive titles special for Piastri |last=McCarthy |first=Dan |date=12 December 2021 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250722041011/https://autoaction.com.au/2021/12/12/three-consecutive-titles-special-for-piastri |archive-date=22 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>}} and the first to win [[Formula Renault]], [[Formula Three]], and [[Formula Two]]—or equivalent—championships in successive seasons.<ref name="SC2023">{{Cite web |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/rise-mclarens-oscar-piastri |title=The Rise of McLaren's Oscar Piastri |date=18 December 2023 |website=[[Silverstone Circuit]] |publisher=[[British Racing Drivers' Club]] |access-date=21 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250521213121/https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/rise-mclarens-oscar-piastri |archive-date=21 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri was named [[FIA Prize Giving Ceremony#Rookie of the Year|FIA Rookie of the Year]] for his efforts in 2021,<ref name="FIAROTY"/> stating "[he had] done basically everything [he] could [to prove himself]".<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-the-most-deserving-driver-not-racing-in-f1-is-spending-2022/9935177/ |url-access=subscription |title=How the most deserving driver not racing in F1 is spending 2022 |last=Karpov |first=Oleg |date=16 April 2022 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240529120511/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-the-most-deserving-driver-not-racing-in-f1-is-spending-2022/9935177/ |archive-date=29 May 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

== Formula One career ==
=== Renault / Alpine test driver (2020–2022) ===
<!-- Deleted image removed: [[File:Oscar Piastri Yas Marina Test 2021.jpg|thumb|left|Piastri completed over {{convert|3500|km|mi|abbr=on}} of testing for [[Renault in Formula One|Renault]] and [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]] as part of the [[Alpine Academy]].{{efn-num|Known until 2021 as the ''Renault Sport Academy''.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/guanyu-zhou-spearheads-five-driver-alpine-academy-line-up-for-2021.6t6Ls79qFgitO7v6j0RSZ2 |title=Guanyu Zhou spearheads five-driver Alpine Academy line-up for 2021 |date=10 February 2021 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250214233352/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/guanyu-zhou-spearheads-five-driver-alpine-academy-line-up-for-2021.6t6Ls79qFgitO7v6j0RSZ2 |archive-date=14 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>|name=RSA}} |alt=Piastri driving the Alpine A521 at 2021 Formula One post-season testing]] -->
In January 2020, three months after clinching the [[2019 Formula Renault Eurocup|Formula Renault Eurocup]], Piastri became a member of the [[Renault Sport Academy]].<ref name="MS2020">{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/renault-finalises-2020-academy-plans-along-with-new-driver-announcement/ |url-access=registration |title=Renault finalises 2020 academy plans along with new driver announcement |last=Williams-Smith |first=Jake |date=28 January 2020 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210802115456/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/renault-finalises-2020-academy-plans-along-with-new-driver-announcement |archive-date=2 August 2021 |url-status=live}}</ref> He conducted his first test with [[Renault in Formula One|Renault]] upon winning the [[2020 FIA Formula 3 Championship|FIA Formula 3 Championship]] that year, completing nearly {{convert|500|km|mi|abbr=on}} in the [[Renault R.S.18|R.S.18]] at [[Bahrain International Circuit|Sakhir]].<ref name="AA2020">{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2020/10/31/piastri-completes-first-f1-test-in-bahrain |title=Piastri completes first F1 test in Bahrain |last=Williams |first=Bruce |date=31 October 2020 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=31 October 2020 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201101134813/https://autoaction.com.au/2020/10/31/piastri-completes-first-f1-test-in-bahrain |archive-date=1 November 2020 |url-status=live}}</ref> He retained his place at the re-branded [[Alpine Academy]] in 2021, for whom he tested the [[Alpine A521|A521]] at the [[Yas Marina Circuit|Yas Marina]] post-season test,<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/de-vries-fastest-on-first-day-of-post-season-abu-dhabi-test/6884875/ |title=De Vries fastest on first day of F1 post-season Abu Dhabi test |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=14 December 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240527064348/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/de-vries-fastest-on-first-day-of-post-season-abu-dhabi-test/6884875/ |archive-date=27 May 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> as well as the R.S.18 again at [[Silverstone Circuit|Silverstone]] and [[Monza Circuit|Monza]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/oscar-piastri-silverstone-f1-test-renault-alpine-20210525-p5isvj.html |title=Australia's Oscar Piastri expected to take part in Formula One test at Silverstone tonight |last=Graham |first=Brett |date=25 May 2021 |website=[[Nine's Wide World of Sports]] |publisher=[[Nine Network]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250424202317/https://www.nine.com.au/sport/motorsport/oscar-piastri-silverstone-f1-test-renault-alpine-20210525-p5isvj.html |archive-date=24 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="AA-MNZ">{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2023/08/31/piastris-history-with-monza |title=Piastri's history with Monza |last=Neal |first=Timothy |date=31 August 2023 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250424202602/https://autoaction.com.au/2023/08/31/piastris-history-with-monza |archive-date=24 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

After his [[2021 Formula 2 Championship|FIA Formula 2]] title victory, Piastri was appointed the reserve driver of [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]] for their {{F1|2022}} campaign, amidst links to an [[Alfa Romeo in Formula One|Alfa Romeo]] move;<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/alpine-no-shootout-between-alonso-piastri-for-2023-f1-seat/6848999/ |title=Alpine: No shootout between Alonso, Piastri for 2023 F1 seat |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=4 December 2021 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240416210807/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/alpine-no-shootout-between-alonso-piastri-for-2023-f1-seat/6848999/ |archive-date=16 April 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> he was also made available in the role for [[McLaren]] following an agreement between the two teams.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-joins-pool-of-mclaren-f1-reserves-for-2022-season/8930177/ |title=Piastri joins pool of McLaren F1 reserves for 2022 season |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=12 March 2022 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=3 September 2022 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240414183830/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-joins-pool-of-mclaren-f1-reserves-for-2022-season/8930177/ |archive-date=14 April 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He completed around {{convert|3000|km|mi|abbr=on}} of further private tests in the A521 throughout the season—part of an "intense" training programme.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/alpine-f1-boss-wishes-piastri-had-a-bit-more-integrity/ |title=Alpine F1 boss wishes Piastri had 'a bit more integrity' |last=Mitchell-Malm |first=Scott |date=26 August 2022 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240624074007/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/alpine-f1-boss-wishes-piastri-had-a-bit-more-integrity/ |archive-date=24 June 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/alpine-intense-piastri-f1-reserve-role/9855692/ |title=Alpine outlines "intense" Piastri F1 reserve role |last=van Leeuwen |first=Andrew |date=13 April 2022 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241013050351/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/alpine-intense-piastri-f1-reserve-role/9855692/ |archive-date=13 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Prior to the {{F1GP|2022|São Paulo}}, he completed a private two-day test for McLaren at [[Circuit Paul Ricard|Paul Ricard]] in the [[McLaren MCL35M|MCL35M]], before entering post-season testing in the [[McLaren MCL36|MCL36]];<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2022/11/13/oscar-piastri-set-for-early-mclaren-debut |title=Oscar Piastri set for early McLaren debut |last=Vasconcelos |first=Luis |date=13 November 2022 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250424201925/https://autoaction.com.au/2022/11/13/oscar-piastri-set-for-early-mclaren-debut |archive-date=24 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he conducted his final rookie test with the team across two days at [[Circuit de Barcelona-Catalunya|Barcelona-Catalunya]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/mclaren-rookie-piastri-ramps-up-2023-prep-as-he-hits-the-track-in-barcelona.1cYJEHUEfdKywoZSsAgNoH |title=McLaren rookie Piastri ramps up 2023 prep as he hits the track in Barcelona |date=2 February 2023 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250218053335/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/mclaren-rookie-piastri-ramps-up-2023-prep-as-he-hits-the-track-in-barcelona.1cYJEHUEfdKywoZSsAgNoH |archive-date=18 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2022 contract dispute ====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2022 Nr. 14 Alonso (misc).jpg|thumb|right|[[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]] falsely claimed Piastri had signed for them in 2022, leading to a widely publicised contract dispute.|alt=Fernando Alonso driving the Alpine A522 at the 2022 Austrian Grand Prix, viewed in a window's reflection]]
In June 2022, Piastri was offered a [[Glossary of motorsport terms#S|seat]] with [[Williams Racing|Williams]] for {{F1|2023}} on a two-year [[loan (sports)|loan]] from Alpine, who were expected to retain [[Esteban Ocon]] and [[Fernando Alonso]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/alpine-piastri-wrong-to-snub-williams-doesnt-share-values/ |title=Alpine: Piastri wrong to snub Williams, doesn't share values |last=Mitchell-Malm |first=Scott |date=11 September 2022 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241014020102/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/alpine-piastri-wrong-to-snub-williams-doesnt-share-values/ |archive-date=14 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> In August, Alonso announced that he would replace the retiring [[Sebastian Vettel]] at [[Aston Martin in Formula One|Aston Martin]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/alonso-to-replace-vettel-at-aston-martin-f1/ |title=Alonso to replace Vettel at Aston Martin F1 |last=Miles |first=Ben |date=1 August 2022 |website=[[Goodwood Circuit|Goodwood Road & Racing]] |publisher=[[Goodwood House]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240806073904/https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/alonso-to-replace-vettel-at-aston-martin-f1/ |archive-date=6 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Alpine then announced that Piastri would be his replacement, in a [[press release]] absent of comments from Piastri himself.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/oscar-piastri-alpine-2023-alonso/10347858/ |title=Piastri to make F1 debut with Alpine in 2023 replacing Alonso |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |date=2 August 2022 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=2 August 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220802161942/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/oscar-piastri-alpine-2023-alonso/10347858/ |archive-date=2 August 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> He rejected their announcement two hours later via [[Twitter]], stating that he had not signed a contract and would not be driving for them in 2023.<ref name="PR2022"/> Team principal [[Otmar Szafnauer]] criticised his actions and "integrity as a human being", stating that he expected loyalty from Piastri and further threatened to take legal action.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-08-14/oscar-piastri-f1-move-mclaren-reveals-major-issues-alpine/101321218 |title=Oscar Piastri's reported F1 move to McLaren reveals major issues at Alpine |last=Doyle |first=Michael |date=13 August 2022 |work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250117210112/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2022-08-14/oscar-piastri-f1-move-mclaren-reveals-major-issues-alpine/101321218 |archive-date=17 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://au.sports.yahoo.com/f1-formula-one-2022-oscar-piastri-alpine-contract-potential-high-court-action-035444736.html |title=Oscar Piastri at centre of Alpine court bombshell amid messy F1 saga |last=Reid |first=Andrew |date=9 August 2022 |work=[[Yahoo Sports]] |publisher=[[Yahoo]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240910134229/https://au.sports.yahoo.com/web/20240910134229/https://au.sports.yahoo.com/f1-formula-one-2022-oscar-piastri-alpine-contract-potential-high-court-action-035444736.html |archive-date=10 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> It soon emerged that Piastri was instead in talks with [[McLaren]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/why-piastris-attempt-to-join-mclaren-carries-risky-implications/10351075/ |title=Why Piastri's attempt to join McLaren carries implications of risk |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=9 August 2022 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240226000626/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/why-piastris-attempt-to-join-mclaren-carries-risky-implications/10351075/ |archive-date=26 February 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

{{quote box|quote=I understand that, without my agreement, [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine F1]] have put out a press release late this afternoon that I am driving for them next year. This is wrong and I have not signed a contract with Alpine for {{F1|2023}}. I will not be driving for Alpine next year.|source=—Piastri via [[Twitter]], denying the Alpine press release two hours later<ref name="PR2022">{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-denies-he-has-signed-with-alpine-to-race-in-f1-in-2023/10347898/ |title=Piastri denies he has signed with Alpine to race in F1 in 2023 |last1=Duncan |first1=Lewis |last2=Noble |first2=Jonathan |date=2 August 2022 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240811113945/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-denies-he-has-signed-with-alpine-to-race-in-f1-in-2023/10347898/ |archive-date=11 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>|width=30%|align=left|fontsize=85%}}
A hearing of the [[FIA Contract Recognition Board]] (CRB) commenced four weeks later to determine whether Piastri was contracted to Alpine, or if he was a [[free agent]]—victory for Alpine could have obligated Piastri to either fulfil the contract for 2023, or required an interested team to activate a [[release clause]] for his services.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-crb-decision-will-decide-piastris-f1-fate/10359998/ |title=How CRB decision will decide Piastri's F1 fate |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=29 August 2022 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=29 August 2022 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220829084729/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-crb-decision-will-decide-piastris-f1-fate/10359998/ |archive-date=29 August 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> Prior to the {{F1GP|2022|Dutch}}, the CRB ruled against Alpine, followed by an immediate announcement that Piastri would instead join McLaren.<ref name="2023contract">{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/62767046 |title=Oscar Piastri to drive for McLaren after Alpine lose contract appeal |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2 September 2022 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=2 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220902135853/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/62767046 |archive-date=2 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> In their final judgment, the CRB revealed that Piastri had signed his McLaren contract almost a month prior to the Alpine announcement—4 July, the day after the {{F1GP|2022|British}}.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://the-race.com/formula-1/ruling-reveals-piastri-signed-mclaren-f1-deal-after-british-gp/ |title=Ruling reveals Piastri signed McLaren F1 deal after British GP |last=Mitchell-Malm |first=Scott |date=2 September 2022 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=2 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220902141558/https://the-race.com/formula-1/ruling-reveals-piastri-signed-mclaren-f1-deal-after-british-gp/ |archive-date=2 September 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref> He was initially only guaranteed a reserve role, prior to the termination of [[Daniel Ricciardo]] in the week before the CRB hearing.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/how-mclaren-did-its-piastri-f1-deal-and-what-alpine-knew/ |title=How McLaren did its Piastri F1 deal – and what Alpine knew |last=Mitchell-Malm |first=Scott |date=2 September 2022 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=2 September 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241008234848/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/how-mclaren-did-its-piastri-f1-deal-and-what-alpine-knew/ |archive-date=8 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri later claimed a "breakdown in trust" between him and Alpine was behind his decision to leave.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/sep/04/oscar-piastri-says-alpine-mclaren-f1-drama-bizarre-and-frankly-upsetting |title=Oscar Piastri says Alpine-McLaren F1 drama 'bizarre and frankly upsetting' |date=4 September 2022 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221129051116/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2022/sep/04/oscar-piastri-says-alpine-mclaren-f1-drama-bizarre-and-frankly-upsetting |archive-date=29 November 2022 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== McLaren (2023–present) ===
==== 2023: Rookie season and maiden podium ====
[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2023 Nr. 81 (1).jpg|thumb|right|Piastri (pictured at the {{F1GP|2023|Austrian}}) debuted in Formula One with [[McLaren]] in {{F1|2023}}.|alt=Piastri driving the McLaren MCL60 at the 2023 Austrian Grand Prix]]
Piastri signed for [[McLaren]] in {{F1|2023}}, replacing fellow Australian [[Daniel Ricciardo]] to partner [[Lando Norris]].<ref name="2023contract"/> On debut at the {{F1GP|2023|Bahrain}}, Piastri qualified eighteenth amidst performance concerns with the [[McLaren MCL60|MCL60]], before retiring from twelfth with an electrical issue.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mclaren-reveals-norris-and-piastri-reliability-issues/10440344/ |title=McLaren reveals Norris and Piastri reliability issues in Bahrain GP |last=Kew |first=Matt |date=5 March 2023 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250401014042/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mclaren-reveals-norris-and-piastri-reliability-issues/10440344/ |archive-date=1 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He started eighth in [[2023 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Saudi Arabia]] prior to dropping outside the [[List of Formula One World Championship points scoring systems|points]] with [[Formula One car#Wings|front wing]] damage sustained in a first-lap collision with [[Pierre Gasly]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-surprised-by-gasly-contact-damage-in-saudi-arabian-gp/10446468/ |title=McLaren's Piastri "surprised" by Gasly contact damage in Saudi Arabian GP |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=20 March 2023 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241127015232/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-surprised-by-gasly-contact-damage-in-saudi-arabian-gp/10446468/ |archive-date=27 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> His maiden [[List of Formula One World Championship points scoring systems|points finish]] came at [[2023 Australian Grand Prix|his home Grand Prix in Australia]], claiming eighth after starting sixteenth.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/piastris-home-race-examined-more-evidence-mclaren-got-it-right/ |title=Piastri's home race examined: More evidence McLaren got it right |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=4 April 2023 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250121121139/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/piastris-home-race-examined-more-evidence-mclaren-got-it-right/ |archive-date=21 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished outside the points with eleventh and nineteenth at the [[2023 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan]] and [[2023 Miami Grand Prix|Miami]] Grands Prix, respectively, suffering contact with [[Alexander Albon]] at the former and reliability issues at the latter.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://au.sports.yahoo.com/formula-one-oscar-piastri-dudded-by-horrible-luck-in-azerbaijan-grand-prix-shame-001655043.html |title=Oscar Piastri dudded by 'horrible' luck in Azerbaijan Grand Prix 'shame' |last=Young |first=Chris |date=1 May 2023 |work=[[Yahoo Sports]] |publisher=[[Yahoo]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250401085030/https://au.sports.yahoo.com/formula-one-oscar-piastri-dudded-by-horrible-luck-in-azerbaijan-grand-prix-shame-001655043.html |archive-date=1 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2023/05/08/major-failure-restricts-piastri-in-miami |title='Major failure' restricts Piastri in Miami |last=Miles |first=Thomas |date=8 May 2023 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=2 August 2024 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230508014847/https://autoaction.com.au/2023/05/08/major-failure-restricts-piastri-in-miami |archive-date=8 May 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> A tenth-placed finish saw him claim a point in [[2023 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://au.motorsport.com/f1/news/piastri-learned-from-following-verstappen-in-wet-monaco-gp/10475506/ |title=Piastri learned from following Verstappen in wet F1 Monaco GP |last1=Kew |first1=Matt |last2=Codling |first2=Stuart |date=30 May 2023 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230613044427/https://au.motorsport.com/f1/news/piastri-learned-from-following-verstappen-in-wet-monaco-gp/10475506/ |archive-date=13 June 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> before a run of three further non–point finishes—in [[2023 Spanish Grand Prix|Spain]], [[2023 Canadian Grand Prix|Canada]], and [[2023 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/why-mclarens-spanish-gp-qualifying-pace-was-a-lie/ |title=Why McLaren's Spanish GP qualifying pace was a lie |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=6 June 2023 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250214214507/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/why-mclarens-spanish-gp-qualifying-pace-was-a-lie/ |archive-date=14 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2023/06/19/piastri-laments-driving-mistakes-in-canada |title=Piastri laments "driving mistakes" in Canada |last=Miles |first=Thomas |date=19 June 2023 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230619091816/https://autoaction.com.au/2023/06/19/piastri-laments-driving-mistakes-in-canada |archive-date=19 June 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/verstappen-makes-biggest-statement-so-far-amid-deluge-of-f1-track-limits-penalties-2023-austrian-gp-report/ |url-access=registration |title=Verstappen's biggest statement yet amid F1 penalty deluge: 2023 Austrian GP report |last=Medland |first=Chris |date=2 July 2023 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=13 February 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230703104705/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/verstappen-makes-biggest-statement-so-far-amid-deluge-of-f1-track-limits-penalties-2023-austrian-gp-report/ |archive-date=3 July 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> Major upgrades for the {{F1GP|2023|British}} saw Piastri qualify third and finish fourth,<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/motor-sports/piastri-deserved-be-podium-says-norris-2023-07-09/ |title=Piastri deserved to be on the podium, says Norris |last=Baldwin |first=Alan |date=9 July 2023 |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=[[Thomson Reuters]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230709223714/https://www.reuters.com/sports/motor-sports/piastri-deserved-be-podium-says-norris-2023-07-09/ |archive-date=9 July 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> before finishing fifth in [[2023 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-07-24/oscar-piastri-praised-by-mclaren-boss/102637656 |title=Oscar Piastri praised by McLaren boss after finishing fifth in Hungary |last=Doyle |first=Michael |date=23 July 2023 |work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]] |access-date=24 July 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230724092859/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2023-07-24/oscar-piastri-praised-by-mclaren-boss/102637656 |archive-date=24 July 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified second for the [[2023 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgium]] sprint, retaining the position after a battle for the lead with [[Max Verstappen]];<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4731492/2023/07/29/belgian-grand-prix-sprint-race-results/ |title=Max Verstappen defeats Oscar Piastri in rain-delayed Belgian Grand Prix sprint race |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=29 July 2023 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250427140343/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4731492/2023/07/29/belgian-grand-prix-sprint-race-results/ |archive-date=27 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he retired from the Grand Prix subsequent to a first-corner collision with [[Carlos Sainz Jr.]]<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://racer.com/2023/07/30/sainz-squarely-blames-piastri-for-first-lap-incident-in-belgium/ |title=Sainz squarely blames Piastri for first lap incident in Belgium |last=Medland |first=Chris |date=30 July 2023 |magazine=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer]] |publisher=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer Media & Marketing Inc.]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=1066-6060 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240217121217/https://racer.com/2023/07/30/sainz-squarely-blames-piastri-for-first-lap-incident-in-belgium/ |archive-date=17 February 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Following a ninth-place at the {{F1GP|2023|Dutch}},<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2023-dutch-grand-prix--six-talking-points/ |title=2023 Dutch Grand Prix {{!}} Six talking points |last=Smith |first=Damien |date=29 August 2023 |website=[[Goodwood Circuit|Goodwood Road & Racing]] |publisher=[[Goodwood House]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241104105653/https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2023-dutch-grand-prix--six-talking-points/ |archive-date=4 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> he finished twelfth in [[2023 Italian Grand Prix|Italy]] upon [[Downforce|front wing]] damage from [[Lewis Hamilton]], taking his maiden [[List of Formula One drivers who set a fastest lap|fastest lap]] after the resultant [[pit stop]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-lewis-hamilton-oscar-piastri-monza-b2404132.html |title='It was totally my fault': Lewis Hamilton admits mistake in Italian Grand Prix |last=Jackson |first=Kieran |date=3 September 2023 |work=[[The Independent]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=1741-9743 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250308091049/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-lewis-hamilton-oscar-piastri-monza-b2404132.html |archive-date=8 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/motor-sports/team-by-team-analysis-italian-grand-prix-2023-09-03/ |title=Team by team analysis of the Italian Grand Prix |last=Baldwin |first=Alan |date=3 September 2023 |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=[[Thomson Reuters]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230926003132/https://www.reuters.com/sports/motor-sports/team-by-team-analysis-italian-grand-prix-2023-09-03/ |archive-date=26 September 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified seventeenth in [[2023 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]] after a [[red flag (motorsport)|red flag]], where he recovered to seventh.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12985648/oscar-piastri-how-mclarens-rookie-has-justified-the-hype-in-his-debut-f1-campaign |title=Oscar Piastri: How McLaren's rookie has justified the hype in his debut F1 campaign |date=17 October 2023 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240203165725/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/12985648/oscar-piastri-how-mclarens-rookie-has-justified-the-hype-in-his-debut-f1-campaign |archive-date=3 February 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Finishing third after starting on the [[Glossary of motorsport terms#F|front-row]] at the {{F1GP|2023|Japanese}}, he became the first rookie to achieve a podium finish since [[Lance Stroll]] in [[2017 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|2017]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.drive.com.au/news/oscar-piastri-scores-first-formula-one-podium/ |title=Australia's Oscar Piastri scores first Formula One podium |last=Misoyannis |first=Alex |date=24 September 2023 |website=[[Drive.com.au|Drive]] |publisher=[[Fairfax Media]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250416121049/https://www.drive.com.au/news/oscar-piastri-scores-first-formula-one-podium/ |archive-date=16 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He then took pole for the {{F1GP|2023|Qatar}} sprint, holding off Verstappen to claim his maiden [[List of Formula One sprint winners|sprint victory]];<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/piastri-safety-cars-my-friend-for-qatar-f1-sprint-win/10530117/ |title=Piastri: "Safety cars my friend" for Qatar F1 sprint win |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=7 October 2023 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240918175351/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/piastri-safety-cars-my-friend-for-qatar-f1-sprint-win/10530117/ |archive-date=18 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> he finished second in the main race, having started sixth.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-57-qualifying-laps-made-qatar-f1-hardest-race-of-my-life/10530641/ |title=Piastri: 57 qualifying laps made Qatar F1 "hardest race of my life" |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=8 October 2023 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240912101905/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-57-qualifying-laps-made-qatar-f1-hardest-race-of-my-life/10530641/ |archive-date=12 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He retired from the {{F1GP|2023|United States}} following a collision with [[Esteban Ocon]],<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.si.com/fannation/racing/f1briefings/news/f1-news-mclaren-reveals-issue-behind-oscar-piastris-us-grand-prix-retirement-sj4 |title=F1 News: McLaren Reveals Issue Behind Oscar Piastri's US Grand Prix Retirement |last=Jogia |first=Saajan |date=26 October 2023 |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]] |publisher=[[Minute Media]] |access-date=23 July 2024 |issn=0038-822X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241213170742/https://www.si.com/fannation/racing/f1briefings/news/f1-news-mclaren-reveals-issue-behind-oscar-piastris-us-grand-prix-retirement-sj4 |archive-date=13 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> and claimed eighth in [[2023 Mexico City Grand Prix|Mexico City]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a45676949/f1-mexico-grand-prix-results-verstappen-smashes-another-record-with-latest-victory/ |title=F1 Mexico Grand Prix Results: Verstappen Smashes Another Record with Latest Victory |last=Horton |first=Phillip |date=29 October 2023 |magazine=[[Autoweek]] |publisher=[[Hearst Communications]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0192-9674 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231105140018/https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a45676949/f1-mexico-grand-prix-results-verstappen-smashes-another-record-with-latest-victory/ |archive-date=5 November 2023 |url-status=live}}</ref> He sustained first-lap damage enroute to fourteenth in [[2023 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/why-brazil-wasnt-pointless-for-piastri-despite-being-a-lap-down/10544308/ |title=Why Brazil GP wasn't pointless for Piastri despite being a lap down |last=Cooper |first=Adam |date=8 November 2023 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240810192059/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/why-brazil-wasnt-pointless-for-piastri-despite-being-a-lap-down/10544308/ |archive-date=10 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> before closing his rookie season with tenth- and sixth-placed finishes in [[2023 Las Vegas Grand Prix|Las Vegas]] and [[2023 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|Abu Dhabi]]—qualifying third at the latter.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/oscar-piastri-unrewarded-las-vegas-grand-prix-brilliance/ |title=What Piastri can take from a drive of unrewarded brilliance |last=Khorounzhiy |first=Valentin |date=21 November 2023 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240811180620/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/oscar-piastri-unrewarded-las-vegas-grand-prix-brilliance/ |archive-date=11 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://au.sports.yahoo.com/formula-one-abu-dhabi-grand-prix-oscar-piastri-telling-admission-crazy-debut-f1-season-031102187.html |title=Oscar Piastri in telling admission at Abu Dhabi GP after 'crazy' F1 saga |last=Reid |first=Andrew |date=27 November 2023 |work=[[Yahoo Sports]] |publisher=[[Yahoo]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250401023913/https://au.sports.yahoo.com/formula-one-abu-dhabi-grand-prix-oscar-piastri-telling-admission-crazy-debut-f1-season-031102187.html |archive-date=1 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri finished ninth in the [[World Drivers' Championship]] with two podiums and 97 points, 108 behind teammate Norris in sixth;<ref name="SS2023"/> his results led to a multi-year contract extension with McLaren until at least the end of 2026.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/66867181 |title=Oscar Piastri: McLaren extend Australian rookie's contract until end of 2026 |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=20 September 2023 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240914202936/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/66867181 |archive-date=14 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2024: Maiden wins ====
[[File:Oscar Piastri Chinese GP 2024.jpg|thumb|left|Piastri (pictured at the {{F1GP|2024|Chinese}}) retained his [[Glossary of motorsport terms#S|seat]] in {{F1|2024}} as McLaren emerged as challengers to [[Red Bull Racing|Red Bull]].|alt=Piastri driving the McLaren MCL38 at the 2024 Chinese Grand Prix]]
Piastri opened his {{F1|2024}} campaign with eighth at the {{F1GP|2024|Bahrain}},<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2024-bahrain-grand-prix--6-talking-points/ |title=2024 Bahrain Grand Prix {{!}} 6 talking points |last=Smith |first=Damien |date=4 March 2024 |website=[[Goodwood Circuit|Goodwood Road & Racing]] |publisher=[[Goodwood House]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241101221741/https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2024-bahrain-grand-prix--6-talking-points/ |archive-date=1 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> followed by fourth-placed finishes in [[2024 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Saudi Arabia]] and [[2024 Australian Grand Prix|Australia]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2024-03-10/max-verstappen-wins-formula-1-saudi-arabia-grand-prix/103306250 |title=F1 Saudi Arabia Grand Prix: Max Verstappen wins again, Oscar Piastri finishes fourth |last=Doyle |first=Michael |date=9 March 2024 |work=[[ABC News (Australia)|ABC News]] |publisher=[[Australian Broadcasting Corporation]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240415101956/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2024-03-10/max-verstappen-wins-formula-1-saudi-arabia-grand-prix/103306250 |archive-date=15 April 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-mclaren-team-orders-completely-fair-in-f1-australia-gp/10591156/ |title=Piastri: McLaren team orders "completely fair" in F1 Australia GP |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=24 March 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240404183505/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-mclaren-team-orders-completely-fair-in-f1-australia-gp/10591156/ |archive-date=4 April 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He claimed eighth again at both the [[2024 Japanese Grand Prix|Japanese]] and [[2024 Chinese Grand Prix|Chinese]] Grands Prix.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://motorsport.org.au/media/news/detail/2024/04/07/piastri-scores-points-in-japan/ |title=Piastri scores points in Japan |date=7 April 2024 |website=[[Motorsport Australia]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250409050529/https://motorsport.org.au/media/news/detail/2024/04/07/piastri-scores-points-in-japan/ |archive-date=9 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2024/apr/21/max-verstappen-f1-chinese-grand-prix-victory-report-lando-norris-second |title=Max Verstappen charges to F1 Chinese GP victory with Lando Norris second |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=21 April 2024 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=13 February 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240529083347/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2024/apr/21/max-verstappen-f1-chinese-grand-prix-victory-report-lando-norris-second |archive-date=29 May 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> In [[2024 Miami Grand Prix|Miami]], McLaren emerged as challengers to championship leaders [[Red Bull Racing|Red Bull]];<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mclaren-surprised-upgraded-f1-car-had-red-bull-beating-pace/10607470/ |title=McLaren surprised upgraded F1 car had Red Bull-beating pace |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |date=6 May 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240522051919/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/mclaren-surprised-upgraded-f1-car-had-red-bull-beating-pace/10607470/ |archive-date=22 May 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri dropped to thirteenth following a collision in his battle for second with [[Carlos Sainz Jr.]], as teammate [[Lando Norris]] took victory.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/sat-mclaren-piastri-more-conscious-of-his-strengths-after-miami-f1-race/10609348/ |title=McLaren: Piastri "more conscious of his strengths" after Miami F1 race |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=11 May 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240920194646/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/sat-mclaren-piastri-more-conscious-of-his-strengths-after-miami-f1-race/10609348/ |archive-date=20 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified second at the {{F1GP|2024|Emilia Romagna}}—demoted to fifth with a [[Glossary of motorsport terms#G|grid penalty]] for impeding [[Kevin Magnussen]]—and finished fourth.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/piastri-excited-for-the-future-after-mclarens-performance-in-imola-as-he.4jq4KJbxxqNUBJKKubBlVG |title=Piastri 'excited for the future' after McLaren's performance in Imola as he rues impact of penalty |date=20 May 2024 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250116024144/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/piastri-excited-for-the-future-after-mclarens-performance-in-imola-as-he.4jq4KJbxxqNUBJKKubBlVG |archive-date=16 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri qualified and finished second to [[Charles Leclerc]] at the {{F1GP|2024|Monaco}},<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13143332/monaco-gp-charles-leclerc-beats-oscar-piastri-to-win-on-home-soil-after-huge-crash-on-first-lap-causes-red-flag |title=Monaco GP: Charles Leclerc beats Oscar Piastri to win on home soil after huge crash on first lap causes red flag |last=Chiu |first=Nigel |date=26 May 2024 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250114161501/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13143332/monaco-gp-charles-leclerc-beats-oscar-piastri-to-win-on-home-soil-after-huge-crash-on-first-lap-causes-red-flag |archive-date=14 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> prior to claiming fifth and seventh at the [[2024 Canadian Grand Prix|Canadian]] and [[2024 Spanish Grand Prix|Spanish]] Grands Prix, respectively.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/piastri-surprised-mercedes-so-quick-canada/10621808/ |title=Piastri surprised "on a mission" Mercedes was so quick in Canada |last=Noble |first=Jonathan |date=10 June 2024 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241007001609/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/piastri-surprised-mercedes-so-quick-canada/10621808/ |archive-date=7 October 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/piastri-battled-career-first-issue-over-spanish-gp-weekend/ |title=Piastri battled career-first issue over Spanish GP weekend |last=Coch |first=Mat |date=24 June 2024 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240714105821/https://speedcafe.com/piastri-battled-career-first-issue-over-spanish-gp-weekend/ |archive-date=14 July 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished second in both the sprint and main race at the {{F1GP|2024|Austrian}}.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/it-hurts-a-little-bit-piastri-disappointed-to-miss-out-on-win-in-austria.SOGcQGLkAeg61iV9od09L |title='It hurts a little bit' – Piastri disappointed to miss out on win in Austria |date=30 June 2024 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250210080040/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/it-hurts-a-little-bit-piastri-disappointed-to-miss-out-on-win-in-austria.SOGcQGLkAeg61iV9od09L |archive-date=10 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> In [[2024 British Grand Prix|Britain]], he climbed to second from fifth in the wet before a belated switch to [[intermediate tyres]] dropped him to fourth;<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5622203/2024/07/07/f1-mclaren-british-gp-norris-piastri/ |title=How McLaren threw away its shot at winning F1's British GP: 'We got it wrong' |last=Coleman |first=Madeline |date=27 July 2024 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=1 August 2024 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240727225629/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5622203/2024/07/07/f1-mclaren-british-gp-norris-piastri/ |archive-date=27 July 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> he fractured a rib during the Grand Prix due to an improper seat fit, which he sustained until the summer break.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-oscar-piastri-injury-rib-mclaren-b2596118.html |title=Oscar Piastri reveals broken rib – which he sustained before first F1 victory |last=Jackson |first=Kieran |date=14 August 2024 |work=[[The Independent]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=1741-9743 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241210085517/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-oscar-piastri-injury-rib-mclaren-b2596118.html |archive-date=10 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri qualified second for the {{F1GP|2024|Hungarian}} before overtaking teammate Norris into the first corner; McLaren then controversially allowed Norris to [[Glossary of motorsport terms#U|undercut]] him prior to [[Team orders|ordering a position-swap]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/jul/21/oscar-piastri-wins-f1-hungarian-gp-after-mcclaren-team-soap-opera |title=Oscar Piastri wins F1 Hungarian GP after McLaren order Norris to give up lead |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=21 July 2024 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250215183155/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/article/2024/jul/21/oscar-piastri-wins-f1-hungarian-gp-after-mcclaren-team-soap-opera |archive-date=15 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He allowed Piastri past with two laps remaining, who claimed his maiden [[List of Formula One Grand Prix winners|victory]] to become the [[Formula One drivers from Australia|fifth Australian to win a Formula One Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://edition.cnn.com/2024/07/22/sport/oscar-piastri-hungary-grand-prix-f1-spt-intl/index.html |title=Oscar Piastri wins his first ever F1 Grand Prix in Hungary in tense race highlighted by McLaren team drama |last=Joseph |first=Sam |date=22 July 2024 |work=[[CNN]] |publisher=[[Warner Bros. Discovery]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241205071136/https://edition.cnn.com/2024/07/22/sport/oscar-piastri-hungary-grand-prix-f1-spt-intl/index.html |archive-date=5 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Norris commented that the result was "fair" and "honest", conceding that he lost the race at the start.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cye03ylnnr0o |title='I didn't give up the win – I lost it off the line' |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=21 July 2024 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=24 July 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241116024719/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cye03ylnnr0o |archive-date=16 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:2024-08-25 Motorsport, Formel 1, Großer Preis der Niederlande 2024 STP 3918 by Stepro.jpg|thumb|right|Piastri (pictured at the {{F1GP|2024|Dutch}}) took two victories as McLaren won the [[World Constructors' Championship]].|alt=Piastri leads Charles Leclerc at the 2024 Dutch Grand Prix]]
Piastri finished second in [[2024 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgium]] after a disqualification for [[George Russell (racing driver)|George Russell]], promoting him to fourth in the standings—ahead of Sainz—before finishing fourth at the {{F1GP|2024|Dutch}}.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-f1s-points-standings-look-after-the-2024-belgian-gp/10639938/ |title=How F1's points standings look after the 2024 F1 Belgian GP |last=Bradley |first=Charles |date=28 July 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240822143117/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-f1s-points-standings-look-after-the-2024-belgian-gp/10639938/ |archive-date=22 August 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cn9l7wn4xx3o |title=Dominant Norris fights back to win Dutch GP |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=25 August 2024 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=13 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240913034843/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cn9l7wn4xx3o |archive-date=13 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He led the majority of the {{F1GP|2024|Italian}} after a first-lap overtake on Norris, before a strategic error saw him finish second to the [[pit stop|one-stop]] of Leclerc.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-hurts-a-lot-after-ferrari-strategy-denies-italian-gp-victory/10650281/ |title=Piastri "hurts a lot" after Ferrari strategy denies Italian GP victory |last=Mann-Bryans |first=Mark |date=1 September 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240909195523/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-hurts-a-lot-after-ferrari-strategy-denies-italian-gp-victory/10650281/ |archive-date=9 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Qualifying second to Leclerc in [[2024 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan]], Piastri claimed another victory following a race-long battle for the lead.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a62211010/oscar-piastri-wins-f1-azerbaijan-grand-prix/ |title=Oscar Piastri Wins F1 Azerbaijan Grand Prix that Features Huge Crash |last=Horton |first=Phillip |date=14 September 2024 |magazine=[[Autoweek]] |publisher=[[Hearst Communications]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0192-9674 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240920194633/https://www.autoweek.com/racing/formula-1/a62211010/oscar-piastri-wins-f1-azerbaijan-grand-prix/ |archive-date=20 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> He then took third in [[2024 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]],<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2024/09/23/piastri-walking-away-reasonably-happy-with-p3-in-singapore |title=Piastri "walking away reasonably happy" with P3 in Singapore |last=Mautone |first=Reese |date=23 September 2024 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241121071041/https://autoaction.com.au/2024/09/23/piastri-walking-away-reasonably-happy-with-p3-in-singapore |archive-date=21 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> before finishing fifth at the {{F1GP|2024|United States}}.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://speedcafe.com/f1-news-united-states-grand-prix-oscar-piastri-results-reaction-lando-norris-mclaren/ |title=Norris made McLaren 'look more competitive' says Piastri |last=Chapman |first=Simon |date=21 October 2024 |website=[[Speedcafe]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241110043943/https://speedcafe.com/f1-news-united-states-grand-prix-oscar-piastri-results-reaction-lando-norris-mclaren/ |archive-date=10 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Eighth-placed finishes at the [[2024 Mexico City Grand Prix|Mexico City]] and [[2024 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo]] Grands Prix—including second at the latter sprint after being ordered to allow Norris to win—were followed by seventh-place in [[2024 Las Vegas Grand Prix|Las Vegas]] after a [[false start]] penalty.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2024/10/28/piastri-on-p8-finish-in-mexico-a-massive-shame |title=Piastri on P8 finish in Mexico: "A massive shame" |last=Mautone |first=Reese |date=28 October 2024 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241107003025/https://autoaction.com.au/2024/10/28/piastri-on-p8-finish-in-mexico-a-massive-shame |archive-date=7 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c75ldl25yx3o |title=Norris wins Sao Paulo sprint after Piastri team orders |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2 November 2024 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241130183854/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c75ldl25yx3o |archive-date=30 November 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2024/11/04/piastri-endures-toughest-outing-to-finish-p8-in-brazil |title=Piastri endures "toughest" outing to finish P8 in Brazil |last=Mautone |first=Reese |date=4 November 2024 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250429114202/https://autoaction.com.au/2024/11/04/piastri-endures-toughest-outing-to-finish-p8-in-brazil |archive-date=29 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2024-las-vegas-grand-prix--8-talking-points/ |title=2024 Las Vegas Grand Prix {{!}} 8 talking points |last=Smith |first=Damien |date=25 November 2024 |website=[[Goodwood Circuit|Goodwood Road & Racing]] |publisher=[[Goodwood House]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241213014607/https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2024-las-vegas-grand-prix--8-talking-points/ |archive-date=13 December 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> Norris returned the favour at the [[chequered flag]] for the {{F1GP|2024|Qatar}} sprint, allowing Piastri to take victory before he finished third in the main race.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-qatar-gp-sprint-report/10677895/ |title=F1 Qatar GP: Piastri given sprint win by Norris in tactical 1–2 for McLaren |last=Boxall-Legge |first=Jake |date=30 November 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250426143756/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/f1-qatar-gp-sprint-report/10677895/ |archive-date=26 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/piastri-reflects-on-painful-safety-car-timing-in-qatar-as-he-prepares-for.4fYPTJU4WbR8HalC9RFesr |title=Piastri reflects on 'painful' Safety Car timing in Qatar as he prepares for constructors' battle to 'go down to the wire' |date=2 December 2024 |website=[[Formula 1]] |publisher=[[Formula One Group]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250323213120/https://www.formula1.com/en/latest/article/piastri-reflects-on-painful-safety-car-timing-in-qatar-as-he-prepares-for.4fYPTJU4WbR8HalC9RFesr |archive-date=23 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished the season-ending {{F1GP|2024|Abu Dhabi}} in tenth after a first-lap collision with [[Max Verstappen]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://racer.com/2024/12/08/verstappen-apologizes-to-piastri-for-abu-dhabi-clash/ |title=Verstappen apologizes to Piastri for Abu Dhabi clash |last=Medland |first=Chris |date=8 December 2024 |magazine=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer]] |publisher=[[Racer (magazine)|Racer Media & Marketing Inc.]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=1066-6060 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250215165035/https://racer.com/2024/12/08/verstappen-apologizes-to-piastri-for-abu-dhabi-clash/ |archive-date=15 February 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri ended the season fourth in the World Drivers' Championship on 292 [[List of Formula One World Championship points scoring systems|points]]—82 behind runner-up Norris—with two victories from eight podiums, helping McLaren win their first [[World Constructors' Championship]] since {{F1|1998}}.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.si.com/formula1/mclaren-signs-oscar-piastri-multi-year-contract-extension |title=McLaren Locks Up Budding Star Driver With Multi-Year Contract Extension |last=Phillips |first=Ryan |date=11 March 2025 |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]] |publisher=[[Minute Media]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=0038-822X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250312051717/https://www.si.com/formula1/mclaren-signs-oscar-piastri-multi-year-contract-extension |archive-date=12 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

==== 2025: Three-way title battle vs. Norris and Verstappen ====
[[File:2025 Japan GP - McLaren - Oscar Piastri - FP1.jpg|thumb|left|Piastri (pictured at the {{F1GP|2025|Japanese}}) was one of the favourites ahead of the {{F1|2025}} World Drivers' Championship.|alt=Piastri driving the McLaren MCL39 at the 2025 Japanese Grand Prix]]
McLaren entered {{F1|2025}} as title favourites, with Piastri expected to challenge teammate [[Lando Norris]] for the World Drivers' Championship.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cddyvmz990eo |title='McLaren the class of the field but have hard tightrope to walk' |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=23 March 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=10 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250401200807/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cddyvmz990eo |archive-date=1 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Three days prior to the start of his campaign, McLaren announced a multi-year contract extension with Piastri until at least the end of the 2028 season.<ref name="contract">{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13326165/oscar-piastri-mclaren-driver-signs-new-contract-extension-until-at-least-2028-with-reigning-f1-constructors-champions-ahead-of-australian-gp |title=Oscar Piastri: McLaren driver signs new contract extension until at least 2028 with reigning F1 constructors' champions ahead of Australian GP |last=Chiu |first=Nigel |date=11 March 2025 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=11 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250312182938/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13326165/oscar-piastri-mclaren-driver-signs-new-contract-extension-until-at-least-2028-with-reigning-f1-constructors-champions-ahead-of-australian-gp |archive-date=12 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified on the [[Glossary of motorsport terms#F|front-row]] for the season-opening {{F1GP|2025|Australian}}, behind teammate Norris;<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c3d8zre0x9lo |title=Norris takes Melbourne pole with Hamilton eighth |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=15 March 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=15 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250315184918/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/c3d8zre0x9lo |archive-date=15 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he challenged Norris for the lead before spinning in wet conditions and leaving the track, ultimately finishing ninth.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cr421xe109qo |title=Norris beats Verstappen in dramatic Australia opener |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=16 March 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=16 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250316070859/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/cr421xe109qo |archive-date=16 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After finishing second in the sprint, he took his maiden [[List of Formula One polesitters|pole position]] at the {{F1GP|2025|Chinese}}, dominating the race ahead of Norris to claim his first victory of the season.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/chinese-grand-prix-oscar-piastri-lando-norris-vbzhtscnj |url-access=subscription |title=Chinese GP: Oscar Piastri claims dominant win with Lando Norris second |last=Hudson |first=Molly |date=23 March 2025 |work=[[The Times]] |access-date=23 March 2025 |issn=0140-0460 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250323113600/https://www.thetimes.com/sport/formula-one/article/chinese-grand-prix-oscar-piastri-lando-norris-vbzhtscnj |archive-date=23 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished third in [[2025 Japanese Grand Prix|Japan]] behind [[Max Verstappen]] and Norris.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6258403/2025/04/06/japanese-grand-prix-f1-briefing-max-verstappen-red-bull/ |title=F1 Japanese Grand Prix briefing: Max Verstappen's perfect win and Kimi Antonelli makes history |last1=Coleman |first1=Madeline |last2=Smith |first2=Luke |date=6 April 2025 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=6 April 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250406081516/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6258403/2025/04/06/japanese-grand-prix-f1-briefing-max-verstappen-red-bull/ |archive-date=6 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri took pole for the {{F1GP|2025|Bahrain}}, cruising to a 15-second winning margin and moving within three [[List of Formula One World Championship points scoring systems|points]] of Norris.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-oscar-piastri-lando-norris-bahrain-mclaren-b2732526.html |title=Oscar Piastri lays down F1 title gauntlet to Lando Norris with victory in Bahrain |last=Hunt |first=Scott |date=13 April 2025 |work=[[The Independent]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |issn=1741-9743 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250415161830/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/f1-oscar-piastri-lando-norris-bahrain-mclaren-b2732526.html |archive-date=15 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He took another victory in [[2025 Saudi Arabian Grand Prix|Saudi Arabia]] to become the [[Formula One drivers from Australia|first Australian to lead the World Drivers' Championship]] since {{F1|2010}}.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6294371/2025/04/20/saudi-arabian-grand-prix-briefing-oscar-piastri-wins-mclaren/ |title=Saudi Arabian Grand Prix: A new championship leader, Ferrari's first 2025 podium |last1=Smith |first1=Luke |last2=Kalinauckas |first2=Alex |date=20 April 2025 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=21 April 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250420235324/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6294371/2025/04/20/saudi-arabian-grand-prix-briefing-oscar-piastri-wins-mclaren/ |archive-date=20 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished second in the {{F1GP|2025|Miami}} sprint after a late [[safety car]] put him behind Norris, before winning the main race.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/may/04/oscar-piastri-wins-f1-miami-grand-prix-to-stretch-lead-in-title-race |title=Oscar Piastri wins F1 Miami Grand Prix to stretch lead in title race |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=4 May 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=24 May 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250506050850/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/may/04/oscar-piastri-wins-f1-miami-grand-prix-to-stretch-lead-in-title-race |archive-date=6 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> On pole for the {{F1GP|2025|Emilia Romagna}}, he finished third after a first-corner overtake by Verstappen and a strategic error.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13370122/emilia-romagna-gp-mclaren-strategy-calls-at-imola-showed-weakness-says-jacques-villeneuve |title=Emilia Romagna GP: McLaren strategy calls at Imola showed 'weakness', says Jacques Villeneuve |date=19 May 2025 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=24 May 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250519053735/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13370122/emilia-romagna-gp-mclaren-strategy-calls-at-imola-showed-weakness-says-jacques-villeneuve |archive-date=19 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He won the {{F1GP|2025|Spanish}} after starting on pole,<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/piastri-wins-from-norris-as-verstappen-gets-penalised-2025-spanish-gp-results/ |url-access=registration |title=Piastri wins from Norris as Verstappen gets penalised – 2025 Spanish GP results |last=Elizalde |first=Pablo |date=1 June 2025 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=29 June 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250629152250/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/piastri-wins-from-norris-as-verstappen-gets-penalised-2025-spanish-gp-results/ |archive-date=29 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> and finished fourth in [[2025 Canadian Grand Prix|Canada]], where championship rival Norris attempted to overtake him and crashed into the [[Glossary of motorsport terms#P|pit wall]], extending Piastri's lead to 22 points.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2025-canadian-grand-prix/ |title=Norris repeats painful McLaren history in Canada |last=Smith |first=Damien |date=16 June 2025 |website=[[Goodwood Circuit|Goodwood Road & Racing]] |publisher=[[Goodwood House]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250723030651/https://www.goodwood.com/grr/f1/2025-canadian-grand-prix/ |archive-date=23 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

[[File:FIA F1 Austria 2025 Nr. 81 Piastri.jpg|thumb|right|A title battle between Piastri and teammate [[Lando Norris]] emerged at the {{F1GP|2025|Austrian}}.|alt=Piastri driving the McLaren MCL39 at the 2025 Austrian Grand Prix]]
Piastri finished second in [[2025 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]] after a race-long battle with Norris, narrowly avoiding another collision after [[Skid (automobile)|locking]] his [[brake]]s at ''[[Red Bull Ring|Rauch]]''.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/jun/29/lando-norris-mclaren-oscar-piastri-austrian-gp-f1 |title=Lando Norris holds off pressure from Oscar Piastri to win Austrian F1 GP |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=29 June 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=29 June 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250629151659/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/jun/29/lando-norris-mclaren-oscar-piastri-austrian-gp-f1 |archive-date=29 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He led the majority of the wet-weather {{F1GP|2025|British}} before receiving a penalty for inadvertently [[brake test]]ing Verstappen on a restart, conceding the victory to Norris.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/why-piastri-was-handed-a-time-penalty-in-f1s-british-grand-prix/10739963/ |title=Why Piastri was handed a time penalty in F1's British Grand Prix |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=6 July 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=23 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250706170855/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/why-piastri-was-handed-a-time-penalty-in-f1s-british-grand-prix/10739963/ |archive-date=6 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He finished second to Verstappen from pole in the [[2025 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgium]] sprint prior to his victory in the wet–dry Grand Prix, which followed an early overtake on polesitter Norris at the exit of ''[[Raidillon]]''.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/jul/27/oscar-piastri-wins-belgian-f1-grand-prix-formula-one-lando-norris-charles-leclerc |title=Oscar Piastri eases away from Norris to win rain-hit Belgian Grand Prix |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=27 July 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=27 July 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250727215100/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/jul/27/oscar-piastri-wins-belgian-f1-grand-prix-formula-one-lando-norris-charles-leclerc |archive-date=27 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He qualified second—ahead of Norris—in [[2025 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]], where Norris beat him to victory on a one-stop strategy.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6533320/2025/08/03/lando-norris-hungarian-gp-strategy-oscar-piastri/ |title=Did McLaren favor Lando Norris over Oscar Piastri in Hungary? Why the team says no |last=Coleman |first=Madeline |date=3 August 2025 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=4 August 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250804162318/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/6533320/2025/08/03/lando-norris-hungarian-gp-strategy-oscar-piastri/ |archive-date=4 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He took pole for the {{F1GP|2025|Dutch}} and held off Norris until his teammate's late engine failure, achieving his maiden ''[[grand chelem]]'' and increasing his advantage to 34 points.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.esquire.com.au/oscar-piastri-wins-dutch-grand-prix-2025 |title=Oscar Piastri takes victory at the Dutch Grand Prix in shock finisher |last=Judd |first=Benjamen |date=1 September 2025 |magazine=[[Esquire (magazine)|Esquire Australia]] |publisher=[[Hearst Communications]] |access-date=3 September 2025 |issn=0194-9535 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250903143319/https://www.esquire.com.au/oscar-piastri-wins-dutch-grand-prix-2025/ |archive-date=3 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Verstappen—104 points behind—re-emerged as a distant title threat in [[2025 Italian Grand Prix|Italy]], where Piastri held third until a slow [[pit stop]] for Norris elevated him to second; he was controversially [[Team orders|ordered to cede the position]] and settled for third.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cx2rn7y5r36o |title=Piastri told to let Norris past as Verstappen wins |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=7 September 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=7 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250907154224/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/cx2rn7y5r36o |archive-date=7 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/needless-silly-our-verdict-on-mclaren-oscar-piastri-lando-norris-team-order |title='Needless and silly'? Our verdict on McLaren's Piastri team order |date=7 September 2025 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=7 September 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250907165723/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/needless-silly-our-verdict-on-mclaren-oscar-piastri-lando-norris-team-order/ |archive-date=7 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/sep/07/max-verstappen-victory-italian-f1-grand-prix-red-bull-lando-norrris-oscar-piastari-mclaren-lewis-hamilton-ferrari |title=Verstappen wins F1 Italian GP as Norris closes gap on Piastri amid pit-stop controversy |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=7 September 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=7 September 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250907163554/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/sep/07/max-verstappen-victory-italian-f1-grand-prix-red-bull-lando-norrris-oscar-piastari-mclaren-lewis-hamilton-ferrari |archive-date=7 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He crashed out of qualifying in [[2025 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan]]; starting ninth, he [[Glossary of motorsport terms#J|jumped the start]], [[Stall (engine)|stall]]ed, and crashed into ''[[Baku City Circuit|Turn Five]]'' on the opening lap, recording his first retirement [[List of Formula One driver records#Most consecutive race finishes|in 45 Grands Prix]] and conceding six points to Norris, as well as 25 to Verstappen.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/why-piastri-wont-serve-grid-penalty-in-singapore-for-jumping-the-start-in-f1-azerbaijan-gp/10761278 |title=Why Piastri won't serve grid penalty in Singapore for jumping start in F1 Azerbaijan GP |last=Codling |first=Stuart |date=21 September 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=21 September 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250921142230/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/why-piastri-wont-serve-grid-penalty-in-singapore-for-jumping-the-start-in-f1-azerbaijan-gp/10761278/ |archive-date=21 September 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> First-lap contact with Norris in [[2025 Singapore Grand Prix|Singapore]] dropped Piastri behind him in fourth, as McLaren clinched the World Constructors' Championship with a [[List of Formula One constructor records#Other constructor records|joint-record six remaining Grands Prix]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/czewkzkjjxzo |title=Norris–Piastri incident 'threatens to derail McLaren harmony'|last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=5 October 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=7 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251006070023/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/czewkzkjjxzo |archive-date=6 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Another first-corner collision with Norris in the [[2025 United States Grand Prix|United States]] sprint saw both retire after Piastri was hit by [[Nico Hülkenberg]] in an attempted [[Glossary of motorsport terms#S|switchback]] on Norris for second,<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/lando-norris-oscar-piastri-mclaren-united-states-austin-b2847900.html |title=McLaren's Lando Norris and Oscar Piastri collide in first-corner sprint carnage |last=Hunt |first=Scott |date=18 October 2025 |work=[[The Independent]] |access-date=18 October 2025 |issn=1741-9743 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251018174840/https://www.independent.co.uk/f1/lando-norris-oscar-piastri-mclaren-united-states-austin-b2847900.html |archive-date=18 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> which neutralised intra-team "repercussions" Norris was set to face after Singapore;<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-mclaren-has-removed-norris-repercussions-after-austin-f1-sprint-clash/10770466 |title=Piastri: McLaren removed Norris 'repercussions' after F1 US GP sprint clash |last=Boxall-Legge |first=Jake |date=23 October 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=25 October 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251025005611/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-mclaren-has-removed-norris-repercussions-after-austin-f1-sprint-clash/10770466 |archive-date=25 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri dropped to fifth in the Grand Prix as Verstappen and Norris—first and second, respectively—closed his advantage to 40 and 14 points.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/zak-brown-glad-to-have-the-weekend-behind-us-as-he-explains-oscar-piastri-struggles/10769458/ |title=Zak Brown explains Oscar Piastri struggles as he's "glad to have the weekend behind us" |last=Mee |first=Lydia |date=19 October 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=19 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251020000658/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/zak-brown-glad-to-have-the-weekend-behind-us-as-he-explains-oscar-piastri-struggles/10769458/ |archive-date=20 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Starting seventh and enduring a mid-race battle with both [[Mercedes-Benz in Formula One|Mercedes]] drivers in [[2025 Mexico City Grand Prix|Mexico City]], he finished fifth again and dropped a point behind the victorious Norris.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/10/27/the-reason-why-lando-norris-quicker-than-oscar-piastri |url-access=registration |title=Lando Norris is quicker but here is how Oscar Piastri can stay in title race |last=Anderson |first=Gary |date=27 October 2025 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=27 October 2025 |issn=0307-1235 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251027160437/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/10/27/the-reason-why-lando-norris-quicker-than-oscar-piastri/ |archive-date=27 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> As Norris dominated in [[2025 São Paulo Grand Prix|São Paulo]], Piastri crashed out of third in the sprint in drying conditions at the ''[[Interlagos Circuit|Senna 'S']]'' and was penalised for colliding with [[Kimi Antonelli]]—causing the retirement of [[Charles Leclerc]]—in the Grand Prix, dropping from second to fifth.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/the-weird-quirks-that-heightened-piastris-struggles-in-brazil |title=The weird quirks that heightened Piastri's struggles in Brazil |last=Noble |first=Jon |date=10 November 2025 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=10 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251110131633/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/the-weird-quirks-that-heightened-piastris-struggles-in-brazil/ |archive-date=10 November 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He was initially classified fourth in [[2025 Las Vegas Grand Prix|Las Vegas]] before both he and Norris were disqualified for [[skid block]] wear, levelling him with race-winner Verstappen.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/nov/23/mclarens-lando-norris-and-oscar-piastri-disqualified-from-las-vegas-gp |title=McLaren apologise to Norris, Piastri and fans for Las Vegas Grand Prix disqualification |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=23 November 2025 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=24 November 2025 |issn=1756-3224 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251124005810/https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2025/nov/23/mclarens-lando-norris-and-oscar-piastri-disqualified-from-las-vegas-gp |archive-date=24 November 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Piastri won the [[2025 Qatar Grand Prix|Qatar]] sprint event from pole position to gain more points on Norris and Verstappen, and finished second in the main race after a strategic error by McLaren allowed Verstappen to win the Grand Prix ahead of Piastri at Lusail. The results in Qatar meant that Piastri who had led the Drivers' Championship for much of the season had now slipped to third in the standings, two points behind Verstappen. At the [[2025 Abu Dhabi Grand Prix|season finale in Abu Dhabi]], Piastri qualified third and finished second. As Verstappen won the Grand Prix in Abu Dhabi from pole, with team mate Norris in third, this meant Piastri finished the season third in the standings, 13 points behind eventual champion and McLaren team mate Norris.<ref>{{cite web | title=F1 - the Official Home of Formula 1® Racing | url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results/2025/drivers }}</ref> Piastri finished the season with seven victories and 16 podiums, both records for an Australian driver. He also passed [[Daniel Ricciardo]] and equalled [[Mark Webber (racing driver)|Mark Webber]] in career victories.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-09-01 |title='I don't do many': Webber's rare Piastri move as Aussie F1 great responds to historic win |url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/motorsport/big-day-for-australian-motorsport-f1-great-praises-incredible-piastri-feat-in-rare-interview/news-story/90bf603a6537e419632858a2833560bf |access-date=2025-12-09 |website=Fox Sports |language=en}}</ref> Piastri's season has been described by himself as one he can be "proud" of, and one of "mighty rise, but uncontrollable fall" by the media.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-12-08 |title=Broken by Papaya Rules, Piastri's brilliant season ended bitterly. What happens next is scary |url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/motorsport/formula-one/f1-2025-abu-dhabi-grand-prix-how-oscar-piastri-lost-the-title-to-lando-norris-mclaren-future-season-review/news-story/c7ba8de59db32682ce1b0b511d855230 |access-date=2025-12-09 |website=Fox Sports |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Waterworth |first=Ben |date=2025-12-08 |title=Piastri 'proud' of season, pledges stronger return in 2026 |url=https://speedcafe.com/f1-news-2025-abu-dhabi-oscar-piastri-result-finish-reaction-interview-title-decider-reflection-thoughts/ |access-date=2025-12-09 |website=Speedcafe.com |language=en}}</ref>

==== 2026: New regulations ====
Piastri remained with McLaren for [[2026 Formula One World Championship#Regulation changes|new power unit and chassis regulations]] in {{F1|2026}}. Having qualified fifth for his home race, the season-opening {{F1GP|2026|Australian}}, he crashed on his [[reconnaissance lap]] due to an unexpected engine surge whilst driving over a kerb and failed to start the race.<ref name="spike">{{cite news|url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastri-explains-cause-of-australian-gp-pre-race-crash/10803288/|title=Piastri explains cause of Australian GP pre-race crash|work=Autosport |last=Cleeren |first=Filip |date=8 March 2026|access-date=8 March 2026}}</ref><ref name="Pia">{{cite news|url=https://www.planetf1.com/news/oscar-piastri-australian-grand-prix-2026-crash|title=Oscar Piastri crashes out of Australian Grand Prix on reconnaissance lap|work=Planet F1|date=8 March 2026|access-date=8 March 2026}}</ref> At the {{F1 GP|2026|Chinese}}, he scored points by finishing sixth in the sprint and then qualified fifth for the race, but again failed to start due to an electrical issue before the [[formation lap]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Saunders |first1=Nate |title=Chinese Grand Prix: McLaren's Lando Norris and Oscar Piastri both fail to start |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/story/_/id/48212034/chinese-grand-prix-mclaren-lando-norris-oscar-piastri-fail-start |access-date=16 March 2026 |work=ESPN.com |date=15 March 2026 |language=en}}</ref> He finished second at the [[2026 Japanese Grand Prix|Japanese Grand Prix]], behind [[Kimi Antonelli]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=2026 Aramco Japanese Grand Prix F1 Final Results |url=https://www.espn.com/f1/race/_/id/600057429 |access-date=2026-04-21 |website=ESPN |language=en}}</ref> At the [[2026 Miami Grand Prix|Miami Grand Prix]], Piastri placed second in the sprint, before qualifying seventh and finishing third in the main race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Miami Grand Prix 2026 - F1 Race |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/racing/2026/miami |access-date=2026-05-03 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en}}</ref> He finished fourth in the [[2026 Canadian Grand Prix|Canadian Grand Prix]] sprint and eleventh in the main race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Canadian Grand Prix 2026 - F1 Race |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/racing/2026/canada |access-date=2026-05-25 |website=www.formula1.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Canadian GP Sprint: George Russell wins as Mercedes team-mate Kimi Antonelli left fuming after going off track in battle |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/33694/13547290/canadian-gp-sprint-george-russell-wins-as-mercedes-team-mate-kimi-antonelli-left-fuming-after-going-off-track-in-battle |access-date=2026-05-23 |website=Sky Sports |language=en}}</ref> In the first European race of the season, Piastri finished fifth on track at the [[2026 Monaco Grand Prix|Monaco Grand Prix]], and was promoted to fourth after a time penalty for [[Alpine F1 Team|Alpine]] driver [[Pierre Gasly]], but lost the position after an appeal that overturned Gasly's penalty.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Monaco GP appeals: Oscar Piastri explains why McLaren are protesting race result after Pierre Gasly podium reinstatement |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13557393/monaco-gp-appeals-oscar-piastri-explains-why-mclaren-are-protesting-race-result-after-pierre-gasly-podium-reinstatement |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260627074642/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13557393/monaco-gp-appeals-oscar-piastri-explains-why-mclaren-are-protesting-race-result-after-pierre-gasly-podium-reinstatement |archive-date=27 June 2026 |access-date=2026-06-27 |work=Sky Sports |language=en-GB |url-status=live }}</ref> Subsequently, he finished fifth again in [[2026 Barcelona-Catalunya Grand Prix|Barcelona-Catalunya]],<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-13 |title=F1 Results - 2026 Catalunya Grand Prix |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/2026/catalunya-grand-prix/results |access-date=2026-06-27 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> and fourth in [[2026 Austrian Grand Prix|Austria]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-28 |title=Austrian Grand Prix F1 race results 2026 |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/austrian-grand-prix-f1-race-results-2026/ |access-date=2026-06-28 |website=The Race |language=en}}</ref> At the [[2026 British Grand Prix|British Grand Prix]], Piastri placed seventh in the sprint race and qualified eighth for the main race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2026 British Grand Prix F1 Sprint Race results: Antonelli wins ahead of Hamilton at Silverstone |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/2026-british-grand-prix-f1-sprint-race-results-antonelli-wins-ahead-hamilton-silverstone |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=Silverstone |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=2026 British Grand Prix F1 Qualifying results: Antonelli storms to pole |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/2026-british-grand-prix-f1-qualifying-results-antonelli-storms-pole |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=Silverstone |language=en}}</ref> He finished eleventh in the main race, having made contact with [[Racing Bulls]] driver [[Liam Lawson]] and sustained damage to his car during the opening lap.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2026 British Grand Prix F1 results: Leclerc wins as Russell and Hamilton take home podiums |url=https://www.silverstone.co.uk/news/2026-british-grand-prix-f1-results-leclerc-wins-russell-and-hamilton-take-home-podiums |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=Silverstone |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Waterworth |first=Ben |date=2026-07-06 |title=Piastri pays price for opening lap damage |url=https://speedcafe.com/f1-news-2026-british-grand-prix-silverstone-oscar-piastri-mclaren-reaction-interview-what-happened-where-first-lap-crash-liam-lawson/ |access-date=2026-07-05 |website=Speedcafe.com |language=en}}</ref> At the [[2026 Belgian Grand Prix|Belgian Grand Prix]], he finished seventh in qualifying, but started the race sixth due to teammate [[Lando Norris|Lando Norris']] ten-place grid penalty,<ref name="Belgium 2026 Starting grid">{{cite web |date=19 July 2026 |orig-date=18 July 2026 |title=Formula 1 Moët & Chandon Belgian Grand Prix 2026 – Starting grid |url=https://www.formula1.com/en/results.html/2026/races/1290/belgium/starting-grid.html |access-date=19 July 2026 |website=Formula 1}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fia.com/system/files/decision-document/2026_belgian_grand_prix_-_infringement_-_car_1_-_change_to_pu_element.pdf |title=Infringement – Car 1 – Change to PU element |date=17 July 2026 |access-date=18 July 2026 |publisher=[[Fédération Internationale de l'Automobile]]}}</ref> eventually finishing fifth.<ref>{{cite web |title=Belgium 2026 – Result |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/belgique/classement.aspx |website=StatsF1 |access-date=19 July 2026}}</ref> Following a three-place grid penalty for [[Lewis Hamilton]], Piastri qualified third for the [[2026 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungarian Grand Prix]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=2026-07-25 |title=Hungarian Grand Prix: Lando Norris takes pole as Lewis Hamilton given three-place grid penalty |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c4gv02vyzv4o |access-date=2026-07-26 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref> He spent multiple laps as the race leader before a collision with [[Carlos Sainz Jr.|Carlos Sainz]], and eventually had to retire on the fifty-sixth lap due to a gearbox problem.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Richards |first=Giles |date=2026-07-26 |title=Lando Norris takes F1 Hungarian GP for first victory of season as Piastri retires |url=https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/jul/26/lando-norris-takes-f1-hungarian-gp-for-first-victory-of-season-as-piastri-retires |access-date=2026-07-26 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>

Following the summer break, Piastri qualified fourth and finished fifth in the sprint for the Dutch Grand Prix.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Netherlands 2026 - Sprint Grille • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/pays-bas/sprint.aspx?grille |access-date=2026-08-23 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Netherlands 2026 - Sprint • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/pays-bas/sprint.aspx |access-date=2026-08-23 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref> He qualified fourth again for the main race.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Netherlands 2026 - Qualifications • STATS F1 |url=https://www.statsf1.com/en/2026/pays-bas/qualification.aspx |access-date=2026-08-23 |website=www.statsf1.com}}</ref>

== Driver profile ==
=== Mentality ===
[[File:FIA F1 Imola 2025 No. 81 Piastri (3).jpg|thumb|left|Piastri (pictured at the [[2025 Emilia Romagna Grand Prix]]) has been acclaimed for his composure under pressure.|alt=Piastri driving the McLaren MCL38 at the 2024 Dutch Grand Prix]]
Piastri has been noted by drivers and critics for his composure under pressure. In {{F1|2023}}, Scott Mitchell-Malm of ''The Race'' compared his "relaxed intensity" to that of [[Max Verstappen]].<ref name="TR2023">{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/three-f1-mega-star-in-the-making-traits-of-oscar-piastri/ |title=The F1 megastar-in-the-making traits of Oscar Piastri |last=Mitchell-Malm |first=Scott |date=18 August 2023 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250116130446/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/three-f1-mega-star-in-the-making-traits-of-oscar-piastri/ |archive-date=16 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Upon winning the [[2024 Azerbaijan Grand Prix]], Luke Smith of ''[[The New York Times]]'' stated that "stress isn't an emotion one would associate with Piastri. His calm, collected demeanor has been present right from his junior days."<ref name="NYT2024"/> This quality prompted several journalists to list him as a favourite for the {{F1|2025}} World Drivers' Championship after the {{F1GP|2025|Bahrain}},<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/04/14/oscar-piastri-lando-norris-world-champion-mclaren-zak-brown/ |url-access=registration |title=Oscar Piastri looks a more likely world champion than Lando Norris |last=Slater |first=Luke |date=14 April 2025 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |issn=0307-1235 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250416031439/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/04/14/oscar-piastri-lando-norris-world-champion-mclaren-zak-brown/ |archive-date=16 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/oscar-piastri-over-lando-norris-rethinking-mclarens-f1-championship-contenders/10713490/ |title=Oscar Piastri over Lando Norris? Rethinking McLaren's F1 championship contenders |last=Hunt |first=Ben |date=15 April 2025 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250416031706/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/oscar-piastri-over-lando-norris-rethinking-mclarens-f1-championship-contenders/10713490/ |archive-date=16 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="AS2025-2">{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastris-cracked-tyre-management-and-quali-pace-now-hes-ready-for-an-f1-title-fight/10713484/ |url-access=subscription |title=Piastri's cracked tyre management and quali pace, now he's ready for an F1 title fight |last=Boxall-Legge |first=Jake |date=15 April 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250416031002/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/piastris-cracked-tyre-management-and-quali-pace-now-hes-ready-for-an-f1-title-fight/10713484/ |archive-date=16 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> with [[Martin Brundle]] comparing him to [[Alain Prost]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/24096/13348951/bahrain-gp-martin-brundle-reviews-imperious-oscar-piastri-win-timely-george-russell-drive-amid-max-verstappen-unrest |title=Bahrain GP: Martin Brundle reviews 'imperious' Oscar Piastri win, 'timely' George Russell drive amid Max Verstappen unrest |last=Brundle |first=Martin |date=14 April 2025 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250416031752/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/24096/13348951/bahrain-gp-martin-brundle-reviews-imperious-oscar-piastri-win-timely-george-russell-drive-amid-max-verstappen-unrest |archive-date=16 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> Andrew Benson of ''[[BBC Sport]]'' stated "combining consistent speed [with] mental solidity and racing decisiveness [makes him] a formidable rival".<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c78jng0q2dxo |title='A fascinating contrast between team-mates and title contenders' |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=13 April 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250414120117/https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/c78jng0q2dxo |archive-date=14 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> After winning the {{F1GP|2025|Saudi Arabian}}, title rival Verstappen stated "he's very calm in his approach, and I like that. [...] He delivers when he has to, barely makes mistakes—and that's what you need when you want to fight for a championship".<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/formula1/articles/crkx7g8re82o |title=Verstappen says 'people can't handle the full truth' after Saudi penalty |last=Benson |first=Andrew |date=21 April 2025 |work=[[BBC Sport]] |publisher=[[BBC]] |access-date=21 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250421021419/https://www.bbc.com/sport/formula1/articles/crkx7g8re82o |archive-date=21 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> As his title battle with teammate [[Lando Norris]] emerged, [[Natalie Pinkham]] of ''[[Top Gear (magazine)|Top Gear]]'' described him as "the cerebral assassin", adding that "he races like he's solving a complex puzzle at [{{convert|200|mph|kph|abbr=on}}]".<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.topgear.com/car-news/formula-one/opinion-piastri-and-norris-are-opposites-so-wholl-win-2025-drivers-title |title=Opinion: Piastri and Norris are opposites, so who'll win the 2025 drivers' title? |last=Pinkham |first=Natalie |date=7 July 2025 |magazine=[[Top Gear (magazine)|Top Gear]] |publisher=[[Immediate Media Company]] |access-date=17 July 2025 |issn=1350-9624 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250707155339/https://www.topgear.com/car-news/formula-one/opinion-piastri-and-norris-are-opposites-so-wholl-win-2025-drivers-title |archive-date=7 July 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> His composed demeanour has drawn several comparisons to [[Kimi Räikkönen]], widely known as ''the Iceman''.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.reuters.com/sports/formula1/ice-boy-no-thanks-says-polesitter-piastri-2025-05-31/ |title=Ice Boy? No thanks, says polesitter Piastri |last=Baldwin |first=Alan |date=31 May 2025 |work=[[Reuters]] |publisher=[[Thomson Reuters]] |access-date=18 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250601110948/https://www.reuters.com/sports/formula1/ice-boy-no-thanks-says-polesitter-piastri-2025-05-31/ |archive-date=1 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/june-2024/88/oscar-piastri-f1s-new-ice-man/ |url-access=subscription |title=Oscar Piastri: F1's new ice man |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=June 2024 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=18 July 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |pages=88–95 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250524034208/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/archive/article/june-2024/88/oscar-piastri-f1s-new-ice-man/ |archive-date=24 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-f1s-new-cool-customer-vindicated-his-mclaren-gamble/10551262/ |url-access=subscription |title=How F1's new cool customer vindicated his McLaren gamble |last=Karpov |first=Oleg |date=25 November 2023 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=18 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240911110751/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/how-f1s-new-cool-customer-vindicated-his-mclaren-gamble/10551262/ |archive-date=11 September 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Development ===
[[File:2025 Japan GP - McLaren - Oscar Piastri - FP1 (2).jpg|thumb|right|Piastri (pictured at the [[2025 Japanese Grand Prix]]) has been noted for his development across his debut seasons.|alt=Piastri driving the McLaren MCL39 at the 2025 Japanese Grand Prix]]
Piastri has also been lauded for his adaptability, with race engineer [[Tom Stallard]] commending his ability to identify flaws in real-time and make improvements without [[data analysis]].<ref name="TR2023"/> His ability to promptly learn from mistakes was initially noted by his engineer in the [[2016–17 Formula 4 UAE Championship|F4 UAE Championship]].<ref name="FS2017"/> ''[[Sky Sports]]'' described [[2023 Formula One World Championship|his rookie campaign]] as "very impressive", noting that his [[Formula One tyres|tyre]] management required improvement.<ref name="SS2023">{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13017184/formula-1-driver-ratings-ranking-the-2023-grid-with-max-verstappen-and-lando-norris-among-the-stars |title=Formula 1 driver ratings: Ranking the 2023 grid, with Max Verstappen and Lando Norris among the stars |date=27 November 2023 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=26 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250313012119/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13017184/formula-1-driver-ratings-ranking-the-2023-grid-with-max-verstappen-and-lando-norris-among-the-stars |archive-date=13 March 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He was noted for his race pace development throughout {{F1|2024}}, as he took his maiden victories in [[2024 Hungarian Grand Prix|Hungary]] and [[2024 Azerbaijan Grand Prix|Azerbaijan]]—the latter was described by Luke Smith of ''[[The New York Times]]'' as a "[[coming-of-age]] drive".<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/general/news/autosport-top-50-of-2024-13-oscar-piastri/10683144/ |title=Autosport Top 50 of 2024: #13 Oscar Piastri |last=Boxall-Legge |first=Jake |date=19 December 2024 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=15 April 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250122203442/https://www.autosport.com/general/news/autosport-top-50-of-2024-13-oscar-piastri/10683144/ |archive-date=22 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/is-oscar-piastri-living-up-to-star-f1-rookie-season/ |title=Is Piastri falling short of his star-making F1 rookie season? |last=Straw |first=Edd |date=12 May 2024 |website=The Race |publisher=The Race Media |access-date=15 April 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250118210510/https://www.the-race.com/formula-1/is-oscar-piastri-living-up-to-star-f1-rookie-season/ |archive-date=18 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NYT2024">{{Cite news |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5768870/2024/09/16/f1-oscar-piastri-mclaren-azerbaijan-gp/ |title=Oscar Piastri's F1 win in Baku was a world-class, coming-of-age drive |last=Smith |first=Luke |date=16 September 2024 |work=[[The Athletic]] |publisher=[[The New York Times]] |access-date=27 April 2025 |issn=1553-8095 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250409100700/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5768870/2024/09/16/f1-oscar-piastri-mclaren-azerbaijan-gp/ |archive-date=9 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> By {{F1|2025}}, several critics opined that he had eradicated the tyre management and qualifying pace issues he experienced in his earlier seasons;<ref name="AS2025-2"/><ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/norris-must-deal-with-piastris-pace-or-suffer-mark-webbers-fate/ |url-access=registration |title=Norris must deal with Piastri's pace – or suffer Mark Webber's fate |last=Hughes |first=Mark |date=24 April 2025 |magazine=[[Motor Sport (magazine)|Motor Sport]] |access-date=17 July 2025 |issn=0027-2019 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250424142519/https://www.motorsportmagazine.com/articles/single-seaters/f1/norris-must-deal-with-piastris-pace-or-suffer-mark-webbers-fate/ |archive-date=24 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13348978/how-oscar-piastri-has-usurped-mclaren-team-mate-lando-norris-as-favourite-for-the-2025-f1-drivers-title |title=How Oscar Piastri has usurped McLaren team-mate Lando Norris as favourite for the 2025 F1 drivers' title |date=16 April 2025 |website=[[Sky Sports]] |publisher=[[Sky Group]] |access-date=17 July 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250425213837/https://www.skysports.com/f1/news/12433/13348978/how-oscar-piastri-has-usurped-mclaren-team-mate-lando-norris-as-favourite-for-the-2025-f1-drivers-title |archive-date=25 April 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/04/22/oscar-piastri-lando-norris-mclaren-max-verstappen-red-bull/ |url-access=registration |title=Data that shows Piastri has edge over Norris and Verstappen in title fight |last=Slater |first=Luke |date=22 April 2025 |work=[[The Daily Telegraph]] |access-date=17 July 2025 |issn=0307-1235 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250517133623/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/formula-1/2025/04/22/oscar-piastri-lando-norris-mclaren-max-verstappen-red-bull/ |archive-date=17 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> he worked closely with his [[race engineer|engineers]] to solve the former and extensively analysed his past performances to iterate upon the latter.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-one-improvement-thats-helped-piastri-fight-for-2025-f1-title/10721193/ |title=The one improvement that's helped Piastri fight for 2025 F1 title |last1=Boxall-Legge |first1=Jake |last2=Vording |first2=Ronald |date=9 May 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=17 July 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250513213652/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/the-one-improvement-thats-helped-piastri-fight-for-2025-f1-title/10721193/ |archive-date=13 May 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/exclusive-how-piastri-chased-his-target-of-improved-qualifying-over-f1-2025/10750616 |title=Exclusive: How Piastri chased his target of improved qualifying over F1 2025 |last=Boxall-Legge |first=Jake |date=14 August 2025 |website=[[Autosport]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=14 August 2025 |issn=0269-946X |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250814195946/https://www.autosport.com/f1/news/exclusive-how-piastri-chased-his-target-of-improved-qualifying-over-f1-2025/10750616/ |archive-date=14 August 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

== Personal life ==
[[File:Oscar Piastri 2025 (cropped).jpg|thumb|left|Piastri with fans at the [[2025 Australian Grand Prix]]|alt=Piastri signing autographs behind a crowd of fans at the 2025 Australian Grand Prix]]
Outside motor racing, Piastri is interested in video games—particularly ''[[Call of Duty]]''—and cooking.<ref name="NYT2023"/> He initially adopted the number 11 in [[kart racing]] before a rival started using it, prompting his switch to 81 in national competition, [[junior formulae]], and as his [[List of Formula One driver numbers|personal driver number]] in Formula One.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-race-numbers-2023-which-driver-uses-what-number/10404332/ |title=2024 F1 driver race numbers: Who uses what number and why? |last=Bekking |first=Casper |date=6 January 2024 |website=[[Motorsport.com]] |publisher=[[Motorsport Network]] |access-date=22 February 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250114132315/https://www.motorsport.com/f1/news/f1-race-numbers-2023-which-driver-uses-what-number/10404332/ |archive-date=14 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> His [[racing helmet]] also originates from his karting career, utilising base colours of red and blue with fluorescent yellow details—modified from [[Ready-to-wear|off-the-shelf]] designs—as well as the [[flag of Australia]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/3mTX3r4YOI8IIaebCyel5O/behind-the-visor-of-a-champion-piastri-takes-us-on-a-tour-of-his-helmet |title=Behind the visor of a champion: Piastri takes us on a tour of his helmet |date=28 December 2021 |website=[[FIA Formula 2 Championship]] |publisher=[[Formula Motorsport Limited]] |access-date=25 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251025002913/https://www.fiaformula2.com/Latest/3mTX3r4YOI8IIaebCyel5O/behind-the-visor-of-a-champion-piastri-takes-us-on-a-tour-of-his-helmet |archive-date=25 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He is a supporter of the Melbourne-based [[Australian rules football]] club [[Richmond Football Club|Richmond]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theage.com.au/sport/afl/the-tiger-who-raced-on-oscar-piastri-s-team-20230404-p5cxul.html |url-access=subscription |title=The Tiger who raced on Piastri's team |last=Ryan |first=Peter |date=4 April 2023 |work=[[The Age]] |publisher=[[Nine Entertainment]] |access-date=14 October 2025 |issn=0312-6307 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250122070636/https://www.theage.com.au/sport/afl/the-tiger-who-raced-on-oscar-piastri-s-team-20230404-p5cxul.html |archive-date=22 January 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> He also plays [[cricket]], where he supports the [[Australia national cricket team|Australia national team]] and the [[Delhi Capitals]] in the [[Indian Premier League]]—the latter after a [[social media]] post asking for recommendations of which team to support;<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.freepressjournal.in/sports/viral-pics-mclaren-f1-driver-oscar-piastri-shows-support-for-delhi-capitals-dons-jersey-no81 |title=Viral Pics: McLaren F1 Driver Oscar Piastri Shows Support For Delhi Capitals, Dons Jersey No.81 |last=Singh |first=Aakash |date=25 April 2024 |work=[[The Free Press Journal]] |publisher=[[The Free Press Journal|Indian National Press]] |access-date=14 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240509044404/https://www.freepressjournal.in/amp/sports/viral-pics-mclaren-f1-driver-oscar-piastri-shows-support-for-delhi-capitals-dons-jersey-no81 |archive-date=9 May 2024 |url-status=live}}</ref> he hosted the national team at the [[McLaren Technology Centre]] (MTC) following the [[2025 ICC World Test Championship final]].<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://autoaction.com.au/2025/05/28/piastri-to-grow-aussie-cricket-connection |title=Piastri to grow Aussie cricket connection |last=Miles |first=Thomas |date=28 May 2025 |magazine=[[Auto Action]] |access-date=14 October 2025 |issn=2204-9924 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251014142626/https://autoaction.com.au/2025/05/28/piastri-to-grow-aussie-cricket-connection |archive-date=14 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Since 2018, Piastri has been in a relationship with his [[childhood sweetheart]], Lily Zneimer, an [[engineering]] graduate he met while studying at his [[sixth form]] in England.<ref>{{Cite magazine |url=https://people.com/who-is-lily-zneimer-oscar-piatri-8598691 |title=Who Is Oscar Piastri's Girlfriend? All About Lily Zneimer |last=Gera |first=Makena |date=2 June 2025 |magazine=[[People (magazine)|People]] |publisher=[[People Inc.]] |access-date=14 October 2025 |issn=0093-7673 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250618021455/https://people.com/who-is-lily-zneimer-oscar-piatri-8598691 |archive-date=18 June 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref> During his early career, he lived in an apartment in proximity to the MTC in [[Woking]],<ref name="NYT2023"/> before moving to [[Monte Carlo]] in 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.kymillman.com/blog/where-do-f1-drivers-live-the-monaco-effect/ |title=Where Do F1 Drivers Live? The Monaco Effect |last=Illman |first=Kim |date=11 March 2025 |website=[[Kym Illman]] |access-date=14 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251014143810/https://www.kymillman.com/blog/where-do-f1-drivers-live-the-monaco-effect/ |archive-date=14 October 2025 |url-status=live}}</ref>

